Decode the actual NODE_HANG ARM event model phase separately from its command
boundary. Require precisely the produced ARM phase for NODE_HANG and retain
the existing range checks for every other producer and all envelope identity
checks. Extend the real initialized ordinary-system fixture with its genuine
unconsumed event round-trip and independently compiled ARM-omission,
unknown-phase and wrong-producer controls. Preserve the existing ordinary
registration, pending and storage assertions and their omission controls.
This is an ordinary event-codec correction, not aggregate restore, selected
Source admission or launched lifecycle qualification.

Exercise the complete ordinary fault aggregate through actual device VMState,
with real zero-instruction RR genesis, requested control boundary and drained
synchronous stop. Configure the realized ordinary generation and register,
clock, hardware and interrupt manifests through their actual public APIs.
Retain a genuine NODE_HANG rule, unconsumed ARM event and queued remove command;
save and reload the full device stream and compare exact event fields/bytes.
Observe actual restored pending handoff, validation and staging physical
journals before dispatching remove. Independently rebuild omitted staging
return and queue handoff writes, retaining every prior ordinary predicate and
physical-return assertion and all original limits. These are ordinary aggregate
component observations; selected funding, full handler retirement, deferred
consumers, CPU borrowers and launched Source lifecycle remain unqualified.
Reference returns do not establish whole shared body or allocator destruction.

Retain RR's factual CPU custody in the actual prepaid CPUState/QOM instance.
Acquire its canonical same-thread/process/nonwrapping holder and real QOM
reference before BQL unlock, distinguish physical executor start, cleanup
revocation and execution end, and return the actual QOM hold only after the
