@@ -0,0 +1,160 @@
+Asynchronous Advance receiver and Entry implementation
+=====================================================
+
+This implementation adds the retained recipient/Entry dependency described by
+``crucible-quantum-handoff-proposal.rst``. It does not qualify a class-one
+Original, RR execution, work-unit outcome or module cleanup producer. The
+existing CPU admission still returns ENOTSUP, and selected Source activation
+remains unavailable. The old synchronous fingerprint loan and v2--v5 member
+constructors retain their separate contracts.
+
+The v6 member constructor copies complete 48-byte Advance and 72-byte receiver
+callback tables into the actual canonical member. Exact version/size,
+alignment, complete extents and table/output disjointness are checked before
+birth. The retained Source/member/Runtime identities are checked independently;
+a callback pointer, table capacity or decoded publication supplies no payer.
+
+The real control dispatcher calls receive after the ordinary control callback
+has physically returned, while the same Main/control extent remains CALLING.
+The module must independently retain its genuine pending immutable command and
+preexisting semantic Quantum Original before publishing its acquisition
+outputs. Acquisition may physically retain that Original's view in the command;
+Enter moves that same view and births only Advance. It never creates another
+Original. Pointer/serial outputs and the moved fact are saved before fallible
+validation or independent post. Every returned acquire invokes the separate
+registered Current callback, including negative first and changed output fields.
+No callback runs under the Source registration mutex. Native independently
+reobserves the recipient, complete lender cohort and final immutable publication
+after receive and handoff, irrespective of module first failure. Separate
+fields retain each post; optional module observer calls cannot replace them.
+
+Physical recipient and no-birth return
+-------------------------------------
+
+Before the bounded session read or Issued-to-Acquired CAS, the canonical Source
+receiver retains separate member and Runtime-service debts. The actual installed
+Setup6 session, Source purpose and consumed publisher aliases retain the peer
+relationship. The receiver is not constructed from an arbitrary mapped buffer.
+Its successful CAS consumes an already issued protocol borrower; copied cohort
+and command coordinates do not issue a module Original.
+
+Each actually acquired cohort row has a separate local view journal. These
+views are distinct from the four kinds of bounded record reader. Complete row
+identity and the unused inventory are validated before any view return mutation.
+Each return records attempted, clears the actual local row reference, then
+records returned. The returned-view mask is accumulated from those real edges.
+All entered atomic readers must have physically returned independently.
+
+The narrow no-birth tail requires either actual nonentry of the module acquire
+callback or independently authenticated known absence from both the real
+acquire and Current callbacks. Negative status and NULL outputs alone are not
+sufficient. Any moved Original, entered Advance constructor, partial output or
+uncertain birth retains the genuine module cleanup path and every parent.
+
+The same physical control return enters a canonical factual tail. It publishes
+zero outcome/units/work coordinates, the actual returned row-view mask and no
+fabricated physical-child bits. One odd/even return publication is followed by
+one exact Acquired-to-ReturnRequested CAS. First/post are retained independently; bounded terminal polls also preserve
+prior busy/refusal and stage-specific return/terminal post facts;
+a later refusal cannot repeat the publication or resurrect returned views. This
+tail performs no callback, wait, notification syscall or new operation.
+
+A later actual control callback's physical return may enter a new factual
+observation frame against that retained journal. Pending, stale, mismatched or
+uncertain observations retain all parents. Exact immutable command and saved
+return words, the authenticated producer terminal record, complete consumed
+membership inventory and command-consumption generation join before the sole
+Consumed-to-Closed CAS. Producer consumption and local Closed are separate
+facts. Only successful physical local closure clears both canonical recipient
+holders and the session operation debt; Source then returns its member/service
+debts. This never supplies semantic permission or reuses Setup's expired clock.
+
+Implemented interface scope
+---------------------------
+
+The implemented new SDK symbols are:
+
+* ``qemu_plugin_crucible_startup_source_command_member_create_v6``;
+* ``qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_receiver_observe_v1``;
+* ``qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_command_observe_v1``;
+* ``qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_entry_observe_v1``.
+
+Their actual Native/Source counterparts authenticate canonical callback fields,
+process/thread/nonwrapping serials, the physically entered Main/control parent,
+retained installed session and the same complete publication. Observation
+outputs are copies for independent module corroboration, never operation
+issuers. Both current cuts run independently; output is published only if both
+succeed. Exclusive observation frames use actual masking receipts rather than
+recursing through Current or borrowing the outer Main-top predicate.
+
+The proposal's Use, Outcome, CleanupUse and CleanupTail observer declarations
+remain contracts for subsequent actual producer cuts. This implementation
+supplies no bodies or accepting/ENOKEY placeholders for them. External modules
+must not link or call those unimplemented symbols. Real RR/CPU children and
+retired-ceiling/next-idle outcome production require their own genuine issuance;
+partial-birth cleanup requires the independently entered retained module guard.
+The full asynchronous module interface is therefore not qualified for import as
+an accepting execution path by this receiver/Entry checkpoint.
+
+Measured prebirth storage
+------------------------
+
+The source-built LP64 baseline is exactly commit
+``a61336a40e156ce3a0fad5a3e9a35f336fe07356``, tree
+``da1615d6086af9b64050310453ed2b0e456f2ece``. Baseline Source/member/service
+are 230032/568/248 bytes and session/storage-purpose are 12648/12760 bytes.
+The following branch-local measurements exclude subsequent mapping,
+construction-read and group-closure histories. Their final union must be
+remeasured before any cumulative pricing or executable claim. Current layouts
+and deltas from that exact baseline are:
+
+========================================= ========= ===============
+Actual record                             Bytes     Change
