+Architecture register reads preserve a negative result before writing
+candidate bytes.  GDB returns zero before appending any bytes.  KVM and
+MSHV register-installation functions propagate the negative result
+before their host register calls.  Runtime paths whose existing return
+types cannot carry a refusal report the error and abort before narrowing,
+shifting or storing that result.  They neither retry the getter nor
+publish an unsigned representation of its error.
