+one allocator implementation. Owned geometry is checked before reserve:
+nonzero page-aligned payload, power-of-two alignment, and checked payload,
+alignment and guard extents. The journal records actual reserve, activation,
+prefix/suffix trim and final installation independently. Only successful
+physical trims change its remaining reservation address and extent.
+
+A failed activation or trim retains its original first outcome separately
+from cleanup. Cleanup attempts exactly one real unmap of the remaining
+reservation. A failed unmap retains that exact extent and negative result;
+subsequent calls return the saved result without repeating the syscall.
+Successful cleanup does not erase the constructor's earlier failure. The
+journal is canonical and process-bound. Copying it, reusing occupied storage,
+or returning it in another process cannot issue a physical return.
+
+Before mmap, the real RAM-list mutex serializes enrollment in a fixed
+64-slot producer registry. This is an explicit finite physical-enrollment
+budget, not a CPU-count assumption or selected byte payer. Exhausted slots
+or the nonwrapping serial leave ordinary allocation on its existing unowned
+path; such allocation cannot subsequently issue an owned mapping child.
+Actual RAM-list insertion records installation entry, and successful
+allocation return completes it only after independently checking the actual
+mapping journal. The later borrower also checks the installed reciprocal
+RAMBlock/MemoryRegion relation, exact producer serial/process, and range.
+No copied tuple or caller-provided pointer can enroll a producer.
+
+The mapping child joins the actual retained resize/discard chunk under the
+same RAM-list mutex. Physical return consumes that child before discard,
+resize, region and QOM returns. Disposal refuses active mapping readers.
+The real RCU reclaim body performs checked one-attempt unmap, authenticates
+its external producer row, and keeps that row occupied through actual
+RAMBlock free. Only the saved external index is used afterward; it never
+dereferences the freed block. An uncertain unmap aborts this void destructor
+before freeing the journal or clearing its producer. This preserves the
+existing lifetime-violation contract; it does not claim allocator backing
+release or complete RCU frame return.
+
+Actual configured LP64 objects measure the journal at 72 bytes, RAMBlock at
+544 bytes, chunk cursor at 200 bytes, getter loan at 368 bytes and Source
+allocation header at 872 bytes. The 2,568-byte fixed producer registry is
+included in the authenticated native inventory floor; ordinary RAMBlock
+allocation owns the inline journal. These extents are distinct from selected
+allocator funding, which remains unavailable. Later full-executable proofs
+must rebuild all users of the changed RAMBlock layout.
+
+The focused mapping component executes the actual POSIX adapter and shared
+allocator with real mmap/munmap. Negative syscall injections refuse before
+that effect. Independent prefix and suffix failures retain the exact original
+or prefix-trimmed range, including a separately failed cleanup and no retry.
+Real kernel-selected geometry, bounded spacer allocations and a fixed attempt
+limit are used; successful syscall results are never fabricated. Copied and
+foreign-process returns, occupied storage, overflow/alignment checks, actual
+physical return and retained failed return are exercised. No populated RAM
+producer registry, Source or Initial Original is manufactured.
+
+The linked ordinary utility/QOM runtime creates an RCU worker before main.
+The mapping component now drains its real callback path and checks complete
+reader inventory before forking. Earlier raw-fork timeouts remain retained:
+an observed non-dumpable positive had sleeping parent/child processes with
+CoreDumping zero. A separate intentional-abort diagnostic observed kernel
+core-dump work, so that is not a complete explanation for the raw-fork
+failure. Intentional-assertion fixtures check process-local non-dumpable
+settings; they retain SIGABRT and the unchanged 30-second deadlines. No host
+core setting or actual QEMU process is changed. The original failures are
+not replaced by diagnostic reruns.
+
+External/file/shared/guest-memfd/CPR/Xen/preallocated/vhost-user backing,
+postcopy/UFFD, RDM, migration/fault-memory and other availability participants
+remain unsupported. Native mapping provenance and disposal exclusion do not
+prove residency or authorize a read. The shared architectural transaction
+still withholds every candidate byte and returns ENOTSUP before a nonzero
+VAPIC read; SDK ENOKEY and selected/class-1 unavailability are unchanged.
+Active mapping-child and genuine Source/Initial/getter execution remain
+unexecuted. The component's no-producer and serial-exhaustion controls prove
+refusal only, not registry installation or a full-capacity fallback positive.
+
+The region read-refusal defect is explicitly paired: it removes both the
+independent missing-producer refusal and the final unavailable-read refusal.
+Either intact guard otherwise correctly stops the component. This control
+does not create an installed producer or admit a read. Its BQL-return control
+likewise removes all four independent BQL guards together. Existing discard
+child omissions now fail earlier at the new mapping prerequisite; their
+expected assertions record that causal ordering.
+
+The unchanged configured preexec generator originally refused the updated
+SDK input fingerprint. Review against its authenticated prior SDK source
+found only additive semantic-v5 declarations and initial-factory comments;
+all seven other authenticated inputs matched. Refreshing that single exact
+fingerprint produces byte-identical literal code. The original generator
+refusal and comparison are retained. This compatibility refresh grants no
+Setup, module, allocation or operational admission.
+
+Mapping checkpoint validation boundary
+--------------------------------------
+
+Fifteen actual configured provider objects compile. Complete focused
+inventories pass one positive plus 18 independently rebuilt mapping defects,
+one positive plus 47 region defects, and one positive plus 34 discard defects.
+Their earlier expectation mismatches and 30-second timeouts remain recorded;
+the later complete inventories are separate evidence, not erased failures.
+
+A fresh matching x86 system target was also attempted with the original
+configuration, source-built tools, at most two compiler jobs, a 6-GiB budget
+and a cumulative 600-second deadline. No retained object, archive or executable
+was reused. Missing configured subproject/public protocol inputs and the
+original SDK fingerprint refusal were preserved before supplying the exact
+unchanged inputs. All required objects then compiled, but the final link
+refused four publisher-action providers missing from this isolated branch.
+Elapsed build attempts totaled 394.884 seconds, below the original deadline.
+No placeholder quartet or older executable was used. The actual whole
+receive/subscription/Main/Action provider cohort must compose first; ordinary
+initialized QMP allocation/deletion, populated producer installation, actual
+RCU reclaim and active getter-child behavior remain unexecuted here. This
+checkpoint establishes the stated component and configured-object evidence,
+not a whole-program, selected, ABI or complete native-suite qualification.
+
+Complete-provider ordinary mapping observation
+----------------------------------------------
+
+A later composition preserves the complete received-delivery, Ready, Main and
+Action publisher providers together with the signed mapping changes. It builds
+a fresh configured x86 system executable; it does not fill the earlier missing
+symbols with substitute providers. The earlier whole-link refusal and component
+timeouts remain separate evidence.
+
+``tests/unit/test-crucible-ram-mapping-qmp.py`` accepts that matching unstripped
+Linux x86-64 system executable, its actual physmem object, and explicit
+``readelf`` and ``nm`` tool paths. It derives private layout from the compiled
+object and observes the actual child process through ``/proc``. Its ordinary
+``machine none`` QMP path creates a private, reserved, preallocated 4 MiB
+``memory-backend-ram``, checks the genuinely installed producer and canonical
+mapping journal, and deletes the same QOM object. Exact QMP bytes, journal bytes,
+process maps and external registry observations are retained under one unchanged
+30-second process deadline. These observations issue no Source or Original.
+
+The real queued reclaim path removes the 4 MiB mapping and its 4 KiB guard,
+then returns the external producer identity. Separate independently rebuilt
+production-body omissions remove the installation receipt, the physical unmap,
+or the external producer return. The ordinary positive and restored-production
+positive pass; each omission fails its distinct physical observation. Registry
+storage is read after deletion, but the destroyed RAMBlock payload is never
+read. Disposal-count observations do not prove that the complete RCU callback
+frame or allocator backing pages have physically returned.
+
+The complete-provider build measures Source control at 229936 bytes. The
+allocation owner remains 872 bytes, getter loan 368, chunk cursor 200, RAMBlock
+544, and mapping journal 72. The actual 2568-byte static producer registry is
+included once in the fixed Source floor. An ordinary allocated mapping and its
+logical producer return do not refund that process-image storage or establish
+selected allocation funding.
+
+This executes ordinary producer installation, QOM deletion and queued mapping
+reclaim. Populated-registry exhaustion, active getter mapping children, initial
+selected callback admission and nonzero architectural VAPIC reads remain
+unexecuted. The selected SDK ``ENOKEY`` and nonzero getter ``ENOTSUP`` refusals
+remain unchanged. This component does not qualify the mandatory launched
+Source/Root lifecycle.
+
+Construction register-read child
+--------------------------------
+
+The selected constructor's real call chain is the initial manifest attempt,
+its retained workspace borrower, the prepaid fingerprint stream, the target
+CPU's ``crucible_register_read_into`` callback, and (for x86 CR8) the existing
+``cpu_get_apic_tpr`` software getter. The stream now issues one canonical,
+process/thread-bound read frame before each architecture callback. Source joins
+that frame to the actual held workspace borrower, its unchanged construction
+Original and Initial participant, and the target CPU's real allocation receipt,
+generation, account and retained workspace QOM reference. Matching scalar
+records or caller-provided storage cannot issue this child.
+
+The callback has separate admission, entered and physical-return facts. Source
+records the callback/no-call result before its independent Original post. A
+negative post retains the read holder and producer frame; neither another row
+nor another stream invocation can replace it. A callback that never returns
+retains the child. The outer borrower, workspace terminal unpublication and
+QOM-return cursor refuse the live read, while a live getter child prevents the
+read from closing. No repeated callback or disposal follows an uncertain post.
+
+The actual software getter also checks the entered read before its own birth,
+software entry and VAPIC prerequisite effects. The getter still requires the
+same CPU's real Initial dispatch: retaining a complete CPU cohort does not
+propagate that callback to another CPU. Runtime Root classes 4/5 are independent
+operations and cannot inherit construction class 0. The architectural getter,
+its five-byte VAPIC geometry and nonzero ``ENOTSUP`` remain unchanged.
+
+The focused read test compiles the actual producer body, ordinary callback
+sequencing and selected prebirth refusal without an installed borrower. Its
+local records exercise only non-authorizing identity/return predicates. Each
+causal defect is compiled separately. These checks do not execute an issued
+Source read, its callback or post, an installed Initial module, a cross-CPU
+getter, or Runtime Root. Configured Source, fault-register, Core, Native, API,
+software APIC and both architecture register objects are compiled separately.
+The earlier ordinary QMP mapping evidence belongs to its matching prior binary;
+it does not qualify these later private layouts.
+
+The remaining installed caller must provide the genuine module Initial
+callback, complete prepaid factory/effect dependencies and the real initial
+CPU construction borrower before the SDK gate can change. For runtime use,
+the registered module's actual Root invocation must lend its own class-4/5
+operation and retained workspace read borrower, with exact producing identity,
+clocks, target CPU participation and independent return/post. There is no
+public accepting constructor for that missing runtime join in this cut.
+Anonymous backing custody does not supply it, or the remaining memory-read
+participants. The SDK still refuses with ``ENOKEY``; activation and nonzero
+selected read availability remain unavailable.
+
+This checkpoint's actual Source body grows from 229936 to 230064 bytes: the
+120-byte read journal and its separate 8-byte nonwrapping serial. The existing
+producer singleton grows from 1024 to 1112 bytes: its 72-byte canonical frame,
+8-byte child holder and 8-byte producer serial. The existing floor includes
+``sizeof(startup_source)`` once and the producer's real fixed-storage getter
+once. Both are static image lifetimes; returning a logical read refunds neither.
+
+Compiled production fixed-floor and transitive getters report 273630 bytes
+before and 273846 after, a 216-byte increase. Every other getter is unchanged.
+These totals already include the prior 2568-byte mapping registry; 271062 was
+the earlier complete-provider base before that registry and is not this
+checkpoint's starting floor. Transitive getters are included through their
+parents, never added again. The measurement-only link retains actual compiled
+getters, discards unrelated initializer roots and issues no QEMU/Source owner.
+
+The concrete constructor entry remains
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_fault_register_manifest`` inside the genuine Initial
+module callback; its SDK begin still refuses before these effects. The runtime
+entry is separately
+``qemu_crucible_startup_source_fingerprint_operation_enter_v1`` inside the
+registered Root invocation. Its exact retained operation, actual target CPU
+participation and workspace borrower still need a distinct entered runtime read
+handoff. Supplying manifest/cohort/scratch tuples to
+``qemu_crucible_fault_register_fingerprints_into_v1`` supplies no such handoff.
+
+Native Initial read membership
+------------------------------
+
+The construction read now retains a distinct inline Native subchild below the
+actual entered VCPU_INIT callback child. Its Source reciprocal first verifies
+the real producer field, canonical holder, live workspace borrower, complete
+CPU cohort, allocation/account/QOM receipts and retained class-zero Original.
+Native independently checks the real Core callback interval and child holder,
+current process/thread, registered top frame and complete VCPU_INIT group under
+its registry mutex. Neither the workspace nor an arbitrary callback address can
+issue this membership. The target remains the actual Initial-dispatch CPU.
+
+The producer distinguishes prebirth issuance from the bound issuing transition;
+the latter is valid only while the actual Source child already occupies its
+canonical field. Native issuance checks occupancy and nonwrapping registry
+serial before mutation. Architecture entry and nested software getters require
+the same retained Native child as well as their independent Source checks.
+Initial callback completion and frame reclaim refuse a live read child.
+
+Return records callback return or genuine no-call separately from Native
+membership consumption. Source records an actual Native return attempt and its
+result before the final independent Original post. That post covers the return
+effect before Source consumes its holder. A negative post retains the Source
+cursor, producer frame, workspace and Initial parents even when Native already
+consumed its child. Reentry cannot repeat that consumption or adopt the retained
+cursor through a new frame. No CPU/QOM pin or mapped backing is freed by this
+inline membership return.
+
+The new Native child is 56 bytes in each of the existing 32 prepaid frame slots,
+adding 1792 bytes to the embedded registry. The Source read journal grows from
+120 to 136 bytes. Source therefore grows from 230064 to 231872 bytes, and the
+actual compiled fixed floor from 273846 to 275654 bytes, an 1808-byte increase.
+The existing 1112-byte producer and its 72-byte frame are unchanged. The floor
+includes the embedded registry through Source once; its size query is not a
+second charge. There is no new heap allocation, mapping or caller-owned scratch.
+
+Focused execution uses the real Source reciprocal, producer authentication and
+Native entry bodies against their empty actual storage. They refuse before
+registry or callback acquisition; fatal linkage guards reject unexpected
+progress. Independent defects also exercise factual identity, occupancy,
+exhaustion and consumed-return predicates. Local records are never enrolled as
+owners. Genuine issued membership, architecture callback, Original post and
+uncertain return remain unexecuted without the installed module/factory join.
+
+The remaining constructor caller is the real module VCPU_INIT callback entering
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_fault_register_manifest`` with its actual installed module
+owner and complete prepaid factory/effect dependencies. The global SDK gate
+still refuses because this isolated construction path cannot fund or close all
+other eager capability factories, GDB/GLib descriptors or their effects. This
+checkpoint supplies no module issuer or substitute provider. Runtime Root4/5
+still needs its own genuine entered operation, CPU participation and workspace
+handoff; class-zero construction cannot supply them. Activation and nonzero
+selected VAPIC memory reads remain unavailable.
