@@ -0,0 +1,344 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+
+Crucible paired parent Park
+==========================
+
+This document describes the local QEMU implementation and its public consumer
+contract. It does not qualify a configured system link or an external transport.
+The checked shared-region layout now binds the published ABI33 header: node
+slots are 768 bytes and the Park return journal is distinct from the action
+return journal. Publisher, plugin consumer and runtime checks are required
+before activation; the historical ABI33 model is not an input.
+
+Production request lifetime
+---------------------------
+
+``crucible-parent-park-begin`` takes ``binding``, ``stopped-generation``,
+``basis-fdname`` and ``cancellation-fdname``. The binding has two 64-digit hex
+strings, ``source-capability`` and ``source-reservation``, and five unsigned
+64-bit coordinates: ``account-incarnation``, ``process-incarnation``,
+``request-correlation``, ``command-frontier`` and ``loan-sequence``. The loan
+sequence must be nonzero, even and below UINT64_MAX. These are selectors,
+corroborated by the live publisher; they never create authority.
+
+The basis descriptor is a sealed, immutable CRUCPDR1/schema1/176 regular file.
+It contains two CRUCPAU1/schema1/80 Original bases at offsets16 and96. Each base
+contains capability32 at16, operation64 at48, original-start64 at56,
+original-end64 at64 and poll64 at72. All integers are big endian. The separate
+sticky cancellation alias must match the live publisher's actual event.
+
+Main receives the original QMP borrower and retains its exact Monitor and
+connection epoch before validation. It then obtains the prepared Source loan
+and retains the real plugin context. The command schedules that same owner on
+the existing paused-main-loop coordinator. Its QMP reply is nonterminal. A
+repeat begin cannot replace an unclosed or uncertain retained request.
+After actual local closure, a fresh authenticated request can reuse only the
+closed per-request storage as described below.
+
+At the real poll cut, after the issuing QMP bottom half returns, the owner
+composes ``request_begin -> metadata_create -> capture_begin``. A census inside
+the issuing bottom half would correctly fail its own active-dispatch checks;
+no counter is subtracted or exempted here. Source observations remain on the
+original received request and thread after the parser issuer returns.
+
+Native closes actual RAM-writer admission, uses that gate's generation as the
+native callback context, and checks the real paused VM-stop generation. Plugin
+acquire must produce a matching held owner. Before CHECK, the real writer gate
+must be drained, RCU and asynchronous reports must be quiescent, and an existing
+independently owned block drain and bound snapshot must be quiescent. This
+request does not manufacture a driver drain or snapshot owner. CHECK runs only
+after these physical facts establish entry. Plugin disposition must report the
+same owner physically disposed before native exclusion can return. Negative or
+uncertain disposition retains the actual gate and request.
+
+``crucible-parent-park-return`` takes only the exact original ``binding``. It
+must arrive on the original Monitor connection. It cannot substitute its own
+parser borrower for the original request. A queued continuation returns
+``-EINPROGRESS``. Native storage, metadata debit and gates must have returned;
+Source then records both final raw Original observations independently,
+including after operation failure. Only afterward can it return the prepared
+loan, plugin context user, descriptors and original QMP borrower. Physical QMP
+return requires the original issuer and every original allocation to be gone.
+Uncertain close, unmap, metadata retirement, plugin disposition or request
+return prevents terminal publication. The same physical loan survives refusal.
+
+Both commands return ``CrucibleParentParkResult``:
+
+* ``status``: retained first operation failure, or zero.
+* ``post-status``: retained first independent Source post failure, or zero.
+* ``return-status``: the raw current settlement result, independently of status.
+* ``received``: the actual original Main request moved to Source.
+* ``entered``: actual native exclusion and plugin acquisition reached CHECK.
+* ``pending``: the real scheduled continuation has not completed.
+* ``native-returned``: this request has no remaining native storage/gate debt;
+  preexisting independently owned subsystem barriers survive.
+* ``terminal-published``: the Source writer confirmed terminal publication and
+  its own local release without uncertainty.
+* ``mapped-metadata-bytes``: exact page-rounded temporary mapping demand.
+* ``completed-requests``: monotonic count of checked local closures.
+* ``lifetime-first-status`` and ``lifetime-post-status``: earliest retained
+  failure and independent post failure across closed requests.
+* Optional ``closed-request``: the Source-authenticated physical closure
+  described below, distinct from terminal publication and operation success.
+
+A reply is an observation, never permission to run or evidence of Source
+terminal publication by itself. Ordinary QAPI errors reject invalid call
+context, malformed coordinates and replacement begins before issuing effects.
+
+Source publication and terminal record
+-------------------------------------
+
+The Source standing record cuts over to CRUCSRV4/schema4. Its extent remains
+1496 bytes; the 896-byte tail at offset600 is absent, Control2, or the distinct
+CRUCPRK1/schema1 Park publication. Park is not an ordinary control receipt.
+The checked preinit decoder generator consumes the same actual decoder bodies.
+This format change requires the external publisher to update; it does not
+change or qualify the shared-region ABI.
+
+The big-endian word at offset196 is producer-retention edition1. Zero and
+unknown editions refuse, as do all predecessor standing schemas. The nested
+standing schema supplies this compatibility boundary inside process-purpose8;
+the standing payload/mapping/carrier extents remain1496/1504/1520 bytes. The
+sealed initial standing record binds the declaration to its installed owner,
+and subsequent records must preserve that edition.
+
+Edition1 promises that the producer retains every born action row, including
+dirty and unprojected rows. An exposed action is irrevocably pending before it
+can match a receiver: unpublished abandonment cannot race a matching request.
+After request publication the exact action birth cannot be replaced until
+its assigned peer authenticates actual local subscription closure. Producer
+death or unknown cleanup does not certify return. Local subscriber closure
+never retires publisher-owned rows; that is a separate producer operation.
+
+This declaration is a prerequisite for a nominal Source subscription, not a
+subscription constructor. Decoded equality, a clean cohort bit and ACK grant
+no membership, operation authority, action Original or physical peer return.
+Ready-stage acquisition and an exact retained Main borrower remain separate
+ownership transitions; Main's BQL-held control boundary cannot take a fresh
+outside-BQL standing snapshot.
+
+Only Source produces CRUCPRR2/schema2/184 terminal bytes. All integer fields
+are big endian; statuses are signed 32-bit errno values. No native pointer or
+native C structure is copied into this record.
+
+.. list-table:: CRUCPRR2 field layout
+   :header-rows: 1
+
+   * - Offset
+     - Size
+     - Field
+   * - 0
+     - 8
+     - ASCII CRUCPRR2
+   * - 8
+     - 4
+     - Schema2
+   * - 12
+     - 4
+     - Record bytes184
+   * - 16
+     - 32
+     - Source capability
+   * - 48
+     - 32
+     - Source reservation
+   * - 80, 88, 96, 104, 112
+     - 8 each
+     - Account, process, correlation, frontier, loan sequence
+   * - 120, 124
+     - 4 each
+     - Retained first status, independent post status
+   * - 128
+     - 4
+     - Phase2: Returned; phase1 is reserved for Pending
+   * - 132
+     - 4
+     - Physical-resolution mask
+   * - 136, 140
+     - 4 each
+     - Planned publication count, locally returned validated pair-view mask
+   * - 144, 148
+     - 4 each
+     - Independent final Original0 and Original1 raw statuses
+   * - 152, 156
+     - 4 each
+     - Operation status, physical return status
+   * - 160, 168
+     - 8 each
+     - Actual stopped generation, actual native writer generation
+   * - 176
+     - 8
+     - Reserved zero
+
+Physical-resolution bits0..7 are respectively the received basis alias,
+cancellation alias, temporary metadata descriptor, charged metadata storage,
+request-owned native gates, prepared loan, original QMP borrower, and plugin
+context user. A bit denotes actual return or a known absence before birth.
+Only the complete mask255 can accompany Returned. A partially validated basis
+has no returned pair-view bits. The pair-view mask returns local received views;
+it does not retire the publisher's independent standing lender or assert
+operation success. Failure can therefore coexist with factual physical return.
+
+The terminal writer's own transient member and Monitor pins are excluded from
+that mask. They remain held during publication and until the writer proves
+local release. A failed or uncertain attempted publication is never replayed.
+The unused historical Pending-only producer has been removed.
+
+Plugin construction and callbacks
+---------------------------------
+
+The exported constructor is now
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_startup_source_command_member_create_v2(id, component,
+reader, writer, out)``. It immediately replaces v1. Both functions bind once to
+the actual component child, independent Bridge, received slot and same Runtime;
+the actual child address supplies userdata. Constructor output precedes the
+independent post, so negative post never discards a born member.
+
+``QemuCrucibleCommandRequestReader(facts, progress, child_userdata)`` retains
+its three-argument signature. Its progress has signed first/post statuses and
+boolean ``read_attempted``, ``request_received`` and ``reader_released``.
+Reader release returns only its local reader borrow.
+
+``QemuCrucibleParkReturnWriter(source_wire, bytes, progress, child_userdata)``
+receives exactly184 immutable Source-produced bytes valid for that call. Its
+progress has signed first/post statuses and boolean ``write_attempted``,
+``return_published``, ``writer_released`` and ``publication_uncertain``. Source
+retains every raw progress field before interpreting callback status. Any
+publication, release or uncertainty fact requires an attempted write. Attempted
+write without confirmed local release retains writer custody. Local release
+neither creates terminal facts nor consumes a material/operation owner.
+
+The existing exported
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_register_parent_park_drain_v1`` remains the registrar.
+Its callback is invoked by the production owner with ACQUIRE1, CHECK2 and
+DISPOSITION3. DISPOSITION uses RELINQUISH1. Matching reports use HELD1 or
+DISPOSED3, with exact schema, size, action, native writer generation, stopped
+generation, correlation and nonzero stable plugin-owner generation. A negative
+callback leaves the output unchanged and cannot certify disposition. Original
+pre/post observations are independent of the callback's signed status.
+Registration alone establishes no entered request. Other SDK exports and the
+C++ ``is_template`` field remain intact.
+
+Storage and integration obligations
+-----------------------------------
+
+Captured-only array branches use separate anonymous mappings. Each nonempty
+array debits ``align_up(count * sizeof(element), real_host_page_size)`` before
+mmap, with overflow and alignment checks. The full raw timer capacity is paid
+before deduplication. Each mapping has its real attempt, raw output, live user,
+munmap result and uncertainty in the canonical request. A failed mmap is a
+known absence, with the raw failure retained; failed unmap retains uncertainty.
+No libc arena history is refunded by these mapped-array returns. Ordinary
+inventory branches continue using their existing GLib allocations.
+
+The preexisting persistent block-root alias keeps its independent owner and is
+excluded from the new debit. Source's actual inline holders and Native's whole
+request, reports, handler continuation and journals are priced by their current
+compiled sizeof in the prebirth floor. No historical request-size constant is
+used. Existing coordinator storage retains its existing owner.
+
+Remaining integration work includes source-built owning translation-unit and
+system/tool/user links, a matched external publisher, consumer adaptation to
+these immediate protocol changes, numerical compiled geometry, and production success/refusal/uncertainty runtime validation. Source
+generation and export extraction do not establish these properties.
+
+
+Local closure, reuse and publisher action membership
+---------------------------------------------------
+
+``closed-request`` is produced in the production return phase only after the
+actual original QMP borrower is gone, the request's plugin-context user has
+returned, metadata mappings/debits and Native gates have returned, the terminal
+writer callback has exited, its writer users have returned without publication
+uncertainty, and the retained Source Monitor reference has actually been
+released. Clearing a pointer before ``object_unref`` is not that release: the
+closure latch is published only after the real unref returns and all other
+physical predicates are checked again. The current return command retains its
+own independent parser and Monitor references; it cannot pay for the original
+request's return or stand in for the released Source pin.
+
+Source checks its actual process/thread and current Main request scope before
+observing the immutable last closure. The receipt contains the complete actual
+saved binding, original connection epoch, actual VM-stop and Native writer
+generations, matching plugin-owner generation where born, Source first/post,
+operation and physical statuses, both independent final Original raw statuses,
+and the terminal writer's callback and first/post results. A zero generation
+can mean the corresponding owner was never born. Presence certifies known
+absence or actual return of every local resource; negative operation statuses
+do not invalidate factual closure. The same exact closed receipt can be
+observed again until a fresh request is admitted, without rerunning its writer.
+A mismatched binding receives no closure receipt. Uncertain publication, failed
+local release or any unreturned user prevents closure and therefore prevents
+reuse.
+
+Only after that checked closure does begin consider a replacement. It first
+observes the actual closed prior request, then reads the authentic retained
+publisher outside BQL. The new publication must be complete, clean and match
+the entire requested binding. Both its even loan sequence and request
+correlation must strictly increase. These process-lifetime high-water marks
+reject exact replay and nonadvancing requests without an unbounded replay set.
+Counter exhaustion fails closed. Numeric freshness alone issues no request,
+Original, allocation credit or entry permission.
+
+The reset consumes only the old request's proven closed receive/prepared,
+metadata, terminal-writer invocation and Native effect journals. It preserves
+the registered member and writer callback, process standing Source/lender,
+Runtime and all independently held permanent metadata debits. The whole new
+Source/Native declarations, including closure history, remain covered by their
+actual compiled prebirth sizeof; there is no per-request refund of that fixed
+floor. Capture and per-array allocation-attempt counters remain monotonic
+across reuse. First lifetime first/post errors and the last exact closure
+summary survive; current request errors begin fresh only after real closure.
+This is a bounded last-closure/error summary, not an unbounded event log. Each
+emitted receipt carries that request's actual first/post and writer results for
+its recipient to retain.
+
+Publisher-side action membership is a separate owner. The current QEMU
+standing/prepared Park APIs provide authenticated read-only publication and
+local pair views, not a publisher-owned membership-return operation or an
+owning retirement witness. Consequently ``publisher-cohort-return-proven`` is
+false in the local receipt. No row state, new publication, pair-view mask,
+terminal writer success or local storage reset is interpreted as membership
+retirement. An authentic publisher can use the exact matching closed-request
+evidence when settling its own actual action memberships, but must perform and
+witness that separate physical operation itself. The process-lifetime standing
+Source remains retained until genuine process retirement; no per-request
+cohort settlement or local reuse retires it.
+
+The owning Source-selected QAPI marshalling and response-allocation path still
+requires source-built integration validation. The report uses the target's
+existing QAPI allocation/deallocation convention; producing a factual closure
+in the native owner does not by itself qualify its complete serialization,
+funding, external consumer binding or runtime delivery. No compiler or runtime
+qualification is implied by this source change.
+
+
+External shared-region header input
+-----------------------------------
+
+The public generated protocol header remains an external build dependency.
+Supply its exact bytes as ``aos/crucible/crucible_shmem_abi.h`` beneath an
+explicit compiler include directory. The pinned source is
+https://raw.githubusercontent.com/andyl-technologies/aos/1bcc1aa291e2040d4041ef488e398c0b20b52fe8/crates/crucible-shmem/include/crucible_shmem_abi.h
+(102098 bytes, SHA256
+``1abf79bdef8f1feef9ceac06cb7dc6b7899cba84b93bc68e3e36123f26850f88``).
+Preserve its ``MIT OR Apache-2.0`` license and complete generated contents.
+QEMU does not carry a second tracked copy of this protocol.
+
+Regenerate the private checked geometry with::
+
+  python3 scripts/gen-crucible-shared-region-layout.py \
+    <external-include>/aos/crucible/crucible_shmem_abi.h \
+    include/qemu/crucible-shared-region-layout.h
+
+The generator rejects a missing or different input before emitting output.
+It consumes constants from that exact header rather than a separate model.
+The resulting static assertions bind ABI33, 768-byte node slots, the action
+hold at offset256, action return at264 and separate Park return at512, plus every
+public factor used by the checked region equations. The fixed node extent is
+24576 bytes, so frame ring headers start at24832. Existing checked arithmetic
+propagates that actual extent through every subsequent region offset.
+
+This source binding alone does not prove that an external writer publishes
+CRUCPRR2 correctly, that a matched consumer authenticates its journal, or that
+the complete system links and runs with the supplied include directory.
