+Registered pending Quantum constructor child: proposal
+=====================================================
+
+This additive process-private SDK contract implements Source constructor-child
+custody, not a semantic issuer or a wire edition. Its exact signed baseline is
+``5c48b36435fb0a2a5861d148d5984a1b83d544b7``. The frozen v2 through v6 tables,
+receiver Acquire/Enter distinction and synchronous fingerprint semantics stay
+unchanged. Source CPU admission remains ENOTSUP. A physical RR/Core frame is
+not a class-one or class-six Original.
+
+Existing gap and actual parent
+------------------------------
+
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_command_lend_v1`` retains the actual
+Source/member/Runtime, Setup6 recipient, class-one publication and complete
+cohort before exposing its canonical Runtime holder. Before ReceiverAcquire,
+however, ``advance_module_outputs_absent`` can still be true while the module
+has partially entered its real Quantum constructor. The current lender return
+cannot observe that debt. Null receiver outputs cannot prove its absence.
+
+The proposed child belongs to that actual lender, not to a copied command. Its
+birth requires the existing lender's complete physical and semantic checks.
+It lends the retained operation to the genuine module constructor; it creates
+no Original, origin, replacement guard, timer, Advance or execution permission.
+The module's actual pending Quantum branch supplies semantic class. Its real
+Core constructor must borrow the existing cohort operation without changing
+the operation's origin, policy or clock contract.
+
+Additive registration and invocation
+-----------------------------------
+
+The two new names are true opaque C tags::
+
+    typedef struct QemuCrucibleSourcePendingQuantumConstructor
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingQuantumConstructor;
+    typedef struct QemuCrucibleModulePendingQuantum
+        QemuCrucibleModulePendingQuantum;
+
+An actual installing module registers three callbacks against its already
+retained v6 member and complete paid Runtime. Registration copies the table
+before its independent installing post and retains negative registration facts.
+The observation is an exclusive prepaid Runtime field outside the contiguous
+complete module wrapper/Core/Advance/cleanup journal span and outside canonical
+Source fields. Both spans require checked complete in-Runtime geometry, not a
+caller capacity as payment. Only the exact registered observation address is
+accepted by observe. Registration does not create a constructor child::
+
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_constructor_register_v1(
+        qemu_plugin_id_t id,
+        QemuCrucibleCommandConsumerMember *member,
+        const struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_callbacks_v1 *table,
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingQuantumConstructor **runtime_holder,
+        uint64_t *runtime_epoch,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_observation_v1 *runtime_observation,
+        void *module_journal, size_t module_journal_bytes,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_registration_v1 *out);
+
+The table has uint32_t schema_version and struct_size followed by the three
+function pointers below, in this order. Version is 1; LP64 size is 32, alignment
+8. Every callback is mandatory. The existing v6 member's actual Runtime
+relationship supplies userdata; registration accepts no replacement userdata::
+
+    typedef int (*QemuCrucibleModulePendingQuantumConstructV1)(
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingQuantumConstructor *constructor,
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingCommandLender *lender, uint64_t lender_serial,
+        QemuCrucibleModulePendingQuantum **module_holder,
+        uint64_t *module_serial,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_receipt_v1 *receipt,
+        void *userdata);
+
+    typedef int (*QemuCrucibleModulePendingQuantumCurrentV1)(
+        QemuCrucibleModulePendingQuantum **module_holder,
+        uint64_t module_serial,
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingQuantumConstructor *constructor,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_receipt_v1 *receipt,
+        void *userdata);
+
+    typedef int (*QemuCrucibleModulePendingQuantumReturnedCurrentV1)(
+        QemuCrucibleModulePendingQuantum **module_holder,
+        uint64_t module_serial,
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingQuantumConstructor *constructor,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_receipt_v1 *receipt,
+        void *userdata);
+
+The ordinary control callback invokes Source, which invokes the registered
+constructor under the actual canonical receiver callback mask::
+
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_constructor_enter_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingCommandLender *lender, uint64_t lender_serial,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_disposition_v1 *out);
+
+The module must release any Runtime mutex or exclusive language borrow needed
+by the reciprocal callback before calling this function. Source holds neither
+the Source registry mutex nor the Native service mutex across any callback.
+The actual Native callback-mask producer authenticates the entered callback;
+the outer Main-top predicate is not a substitute while that mask is entered.
+
+Before invoking construct, Source publishes its actual inline child and fresh
+nonwrapping epoch into the registered Runtime fields, links the actual lender
+and member, and records construct entry. This is before any module constructor
+post can fail. The callback must publish its real prepaid ModulePendingQuantum
+wrapper into the exact ``&child.module_pending`` and
+``&child.module_pending_serial`` before attempting the real Core constructor.
+Those addresses, not caller-selected substitutes, are passed to every callback.
+Source records callback return independently of every semantic or Core fact.
+
+The wrapper must retain its genuine Core constructor/cleanup journals and the
+actual pending branch before any fallible Original entry. A negative callback
+with empty outputs is uncertain, not known NoBirth. A changed output after
+Source saves it is likewise uncertain. In both cases the Runtime's Source
+child holder remains accessible and all parents stay retained.
+
+Nonrecursive observation and independent cuts
+--------------------------------------------
+
+The module's construct/current callback may use::
+
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_constructor_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingQuantumConstructor *constructor, uint64_t epoch,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_observation_v1 *out);
+
+This is a one-way Source leaf. It never calls module Current or another
+constructor API. It authenticates exact Source/member/lender/recipient parents,
+registered Runtime holder/epoch, process/thread, the entered constructor or
+Current callback frame and the unchanged immutable publication/cohort. It uses
+exclusive prepaid inline scratch and independent before/after protocol cuts.
+No Source or Native mutex is held when calling the other layer's leaf.
+
+The observation has uint32_t version/size, then eight uint64_t values:
+constructor, lender, receiver and recipient serials, publication sequence,
+loan generation, ticket serial and callback epoch; then the complete 896-byte
+cohort and 128-byte immutable command. LP64 size is 1096, alignment 8. Copies
+only corroborate the actual nominal loan. They cannot issue a Core operation.
+
+Source saves construct outputs before calling independent module Current.
+Module Current runs even after a negative construct first. Independent Native,
+Source/recipient, cohort and publication-final posts run on every outcome;
+failure in one cannot skip another. Every result has its own retained field.
+Usable output requires all applicable semantic cuts; retained custody does not.
+
+The 56-byte receipt has uint32_t version, size, original_attempted,
+original_entered, original_moved, original_returned, return_attempted and
+local_consumed; int32_t first_status and post_status; then uint64_t
+original_serial and transfer_serial. These describe the wrapper's real Core
+journals. Copied facts alone are never return authority. In particular,
+callback return, Original return and Source child consumption are distinct.
+
+The 48-byte disposition has uint32_t version, size, attempted, held,
+construct_entered, construct_returned, return_attempted and consumed;
+int32_t first_status and post_status; then uint64_t module_serial.
+The 32-byte registration result has uint32_t version, size, registered and
+zero reserved; uint64_t registration_serial; int32_t first_status and
+post_status. Every output requires exact version/size, alignment, checked
+extent and disjointness from all owner journals, canonical fields and inputs
+before any mutation. All three structures have alignment 8.
+
+Physical return and debt order
+-----------------------------
+
+Factual child return uses::
+
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_constructor_return_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingQuantumConstructor *constructor, uint64_t epoch,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_constructor_disposition_v1 *out);
+
+This invokes only registered returned_current, an observation of the real
+wrapper's retained physical-return journals. It performs no Core destructor,
+wait, callback work interval or semantic cleanup. The wrapper stays retained
+in its actual Runtime until the Source child closes, so posts never inspect a
+dead Original. A negative Original first/post can coexist with authentic
+physical closure. A negative factual returned_current, uncertain birth,
+changed holder or interrupted return retains every debt without retrying a
+destructor. Consumed replay reports saved facts without another callback.
+
+During the same entered ordinary callback, the actual physical Main/control
+and constructor-return callback frame authenticate this local closure. After
+Main returns there is currently no joined genuine module cleanup-frame issuer
+for this child: it remains retained. Id/thread equality, a replacement Main,
+the expired Setup guard and the physical RR frame cannot bypass that boundary.
+The eventual deferred path must join the real independently entered module
+cleanup guard before any fallible cleanup, not create one from this receipt.
+
+The child survives ReceiverAcquire and the physical move of the same Original
+in Advance Enter. Its wrapper must follow that actual moved Original's return
+receipt, rather than retaining a second Original. The acyclic order is actual
+Advance/CPU/read/outcome children return, actual Core Original return (or
+authenticated constructor no-entry), retained wrapper returned_current,
+Source constructor child close, pending lender local return, actual protocol
+row/read returns and ReturnRequested, producer consumption, local Closed,
+then receiver/member/service and Runtime retirement.
+
+Lender return independently refuses its exact live or uncertain constructor
+child even before ReceiverAcquire. All known-NoBirth/receiver-drop/terminal
+paths independently require the actual constructor journal closed, even if
+the old receiver outputs are empty. Member retirement/rebind also checks its
+exact registered child. This is nominal holder/epoch identity and retained
+debt, not a bare use count or module boolean. The existing lender retains the
+real receiver/member/session parents throughout; no circular second service
+debt is added. Entered-but-empty construction cannot select the no-birth tail.
+
+Prebirth candidate and qualification boundary
+--------------------------------------------
+
+Actual source-built complete production layout against the signed baseline
+measures Source 240264 (previously 238600), member 800 (previously 696), and
+lender 1280 (previously 1264) bytes. The 104-byte member registration journal,
+16-byte lender reciprocal and 1544-byte inline constructor child increase the
+actual Source fixed floor by 1664 bytes. The child has its three retained
+56-byte receipts at offset 280 and exclusive 1096-byte scratch at offset 448;
+its Source offset is 14192. These replace the earlier draft's 1616-byte estimate:
+24 bytes retain the approved factual Runtime spans and 24 bytes retain the
+actual saved module outputs and registration incarnation. The real compiled
+Source getter includes the complete containing layout through sizeof Source.
+No new dynamic allocation, backing file or Native static frame is introduced.
+The existing exclusive 64-byte receiver callback frame is reused. A later
+cumulative union requires a fresh complete layout and floor measurement.
+
+The real module Runtime additionally needs its canonical Source holder/epoch
+and complete ModulePendingQuantum/Core constructor/cleanup journals. Their
+actual full extent and genuine payer must be measured by the paired module
+implementation; decoded capacity or Source scratch cannot pay them. No callback
+is enrolled merely to obtain a passing test. The real module/Core constructor,
+successful paid Source child, moved Original and deferred cleanup positives
+remain unexecuted until those genuine counterparts join.
+
+Implementation controls must independently remove registration-before-post,
+the lender and each no-birth gate, exact holder/epoch/Runtime extent checks,
+process/thread/frame checks, nonwrap checks, each independent post and the
+physical-return distinction. They must cover partial entry, moved Original,
+negative first with successful factual closure, consumed-negative replay,
+changed outputs, aliasing and dead-Main refusal. Literal physical leaves may
+exercise these predicates without claiming a populated accepting issuer.
+
+Implementation boundaries
+-------------------------
+
+The registered module/Core constructor remains an external genuine producer.
+No callback table, paid Source session or populated Original is manufactured by
+this checkpoint's tests. Before frozen v6 ReceiverAcquire, Source independently
+requires this actual retained child with successful saved constructor/Current
+and a fresh complete Source/protocol cut. The frozen Acquire still retains the
+module's existing Original and Enter moves that exact view; neither creates an
+operation from the observation.
+
+The existing protocol no-birth return publishes zero physical-child bits and
+has no born mask. Therefore the separate no-birth predicate additionally
+refuses any Original entered in construct, independent Current or factual-return
+journals, even after local physical closure. Such an actual early-born Original
+needs its real registered operation-return path, which is not supplied here.
+This is distinct from general physical child closure and retains the recipient
+rather than asserting that a returned Original was never born.
+
+Callbacks are always outside Source/Native mutexes. The Source observe leaf
+never invokes module Current. Current is independently attempted after a
+negative constructor result; Native, Source, recipient, cohort and final posts
+run independently after failures. Saved output mutation becomes uncertainty.
+Physical ReturnedCurrent cannot retry cleanup: an uncertain attempt retains
+the child and all parents. A consumed-negative result cannot resurrect it.
+No deferred cleanup actor, runtime RR actor, CPU/read child, class-six Original,
+selected admission or activation is joined by this constructor dependency.
+
+Scoped implementation evidence
+------------------------------
+
+The production Source, Native invocation, x86 preexec and AArch64 preexec
+objects compile with the configured source-built compiler and GLib inputs.
+The unchanged literal preexec body passes its 34 transport tests. The focused
+constructor test compiles the actual physical leaf bodies and 54 independent
+omissions. Its local positive covers span geometry, receipt syntax, exact saved
+output identity and once-only local consumption; its post dependencies refuse.
+Nine further controls remove literal production guards without executing those
+genuine-owner branches. Neither class of control enrolls an accepting module
+callback or qualifies a paid Source/Runtime/Original invocation.
+
+In particular, controls distinguish failed Current entry from a returned
+Current callback, normalize positive callback statuses to protocol refusal,
+retain changed holder/serial uncertainty in Current and ReturnedCurrent, and
