+Pending Quantum command lender
+==============================
+
+This separate dependency extends the receiver/Entry checkpoint at
+``6f597003260a33822b0226061e0c3eeb0ae695f6``. The v6 callback tables, their
+signatures and synchronous fingerprint action remain unchanged. The new lender
+is a nominal child of the actual admitted Source, registered Runtime/member
+and installed Setup6 session. It issues no Original, Advance, execution
+permission, fresh origin, replacement guard or timer. CPU admission still
+returns ENOTSUP and selected activation remains unavailable.
+
+Actual caller and constructor contract
+-------------------------------------
+
+The genuine module's ordinary registered control callback first selects its
+actual pending Quantum branch under its retained immutable command owner. A
+preparation, reset or fingerprint branch cannot be relabelled. While that
+callback is entered it calls::
+
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_command_lend_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleCommandConsumerMember *member,
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingCommandLender **holder, uint64_t *serial,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_command_disposition_v1 *out);
+
+``holder`` and ``serial`` are distinct, initially empty canonical fields inside
+that actual paid Runtime's complete retained extent. The pending command owns
+those fields through its real Runtime relationship. Passing an arbitrary
+allocation, matching identity or decoded capacity cannot create this parent.
+The adapter selects the actual dispatch Main/control field addresses; the module
+cannot nominate copied tickets. Source independently authenticates the entered
+registration, canonical member/Runtime, process/thread and nonwrapping serial.
+It retains the receiver's actual member/service cleanup debts before the one
+recipient acquire CAS. It authenticates the complete live class-one Host cohort
+and immutable command under that installed endpoint.
+
+Only after that genuine recipient exists does Source publish the nominal
+lender into the exact Runtime fields, before any fallible copy/post. Every born
+negative remains accessible through those fields. No module Original is issued
+by this publication, its CAS or the copied cohort. If acquisition is unavailable
+before local lender birth, the fields remain empty; an acquired protocol child
+and its independent cleanup parents remain in Source even if its post refused.
+
+The module constructor must retain this nominal lender before entering or
+retaining any operation view. Its real pending Quantum branch supplies semantic
+class; the independently authenticated Source cohort supplies the existing Host
+operation's complete lender contract. The genuine Core constructor must borrow
+that same operation, preserving its existing origin, clock contract, policy and
+all cohort memberships. It must not construct an operation from an observation
+copy, a slot flag, matching command fields, the physical Main or Setup's expired
+clock. Its own independent first/post and partial Original/view birth remain
+module-owned facts, with actual cleanup authority retained before fallible
+entry. This Core/module constructor is not implemented by this QEMU dependency.
+
+Existing wake and delivery order
+--------------------------------
+
+The actual Native path is the original registered node wake descriptor:
+``qemu_plugin_register_wake_fd`` installs ``qemu_plugin_wake_fd_read`` in
+``plugins/api-system.c``. After draining, that reader publishes the RR control
+request; settled RR acknowledges at idle, and the two main-loop barrier passes
+call ``qemu_plugin_fire_control_boundary_cb`` under BQL. Its retained registered
+group enters ``control_stop_dispatch`` and the ordinary callback. That callback
+must retain this lender before physical return and the subsequent receiver.
+The immutable publication and Issued ticket must precede the wake that delivers
+this constructor. A scheduler futex wake alone requests no such Main boundary.
+
+Setup6 producer/receiver event aliases are physically retained and identified;
+this dependency supplies no event handler for them. Ringing the receiver event
+cannot substitute for the registered node wake in this implementation. The
+paired producer's protocol notifications and actual pending-command parser
+remain separate integration requirements. ENOKEY for a missing constructor is
+refusal, never proof of semantic absence or permission to execute a command.
+
+Bounded nominal borrowing
+------------------------
+
+The actual pending constructor observes its held nominal lender with::
+
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_command_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingCommandLender *lender, uint64_t serial,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_command_observation_v1 *out);
+
+Version is 1 and size is exactly the corresponding C structure. The observation
+contains version/size, five 64-bit lender/recipient/publication/loan/ticket
+incarnations, the entire canonical 896-byte CRUCACT2 cohort and 128-byte publisher
+command. LP64 size is 1072 bytes, alignment 8. These remain public protocol bytes,
+not a QEMU private layout or an operation issuer. The nominal lender owns the
+retained recipient and its actual row views; decoding or retaining bytes alone
+retains none of those owners.
+
+Source checks complete output extents, alignment, overflow and disjointness
+from Source/preexec/session journals, mapping and canonical holder fields before
+mutation. Its exclusive inline scratch receives the bytes retained before the
+original acquire CAS. Physical Native entry, complete Source/cohort current and
+final immutable command/ticket observations bracket the copy. Each independent
+post runs after negative first; all stage statuses remain separate. An actual
+registered masked callback uses its own canonical suppression receipt rather
+than bypassing the outer Main predicate. Failed first/post withholds the usable
+observation, while the creation holder and debts remain accessible.
+
+The ordinary callback must physically return before the later receiver invokes
+its registered acquire. That receiver reuses this exact recipient; it never
+performs another acquire CAS or creates a missing pending producer. Missing
+pending construction refuses before a new child. The module's acquire retains
+its already genuine Quantum view in its true ModuleCommand and the existing
+Enter moves that exact view; Enter still creates only Advance.
+
+Physical return and retained cleanup
+------------------------------------
+
+Local return uses::
+
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_command_return_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourcePendingCommandLender *lender, uint64_t serial,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_command_disposition_v1 *out);
+
+The 32-byte disposition (alignment 4) contains version/size, attempted,
+retained, return_attempted and consumed 32-bit facts, then signed first/post.
+Every fact describes this local lender only, not peer consumption or completion.
+The module must return its dependent Core views/children first. Source also
+refuses while any registered module acquisition output remains, during an
+exclusive read or after an uncertain return attempt. The actual entered
+physical callback frame authenticates local consumption even when semantic
+current/Original post has failed. The sole attempt clears the exact holder and
+serial, records consumed separately, and then independently observes the
+retained Source/recipient/cohort/command. Negative post never resurrects the
+child or permits another release. Repeated consumed return in the same authentic
+physical scope reports the saved result without repeating consumption.
+
+The recipient, member/service and session cleanup parents outlive this local
+return. A held lender blocks receiver retirement and no-birth protocol return.
+An acquired protocol recipient returns its actual row views and readers before
+ReturnRequested, waits for authenticated producer consumption, then closes
+locally before parent debt is consumed, as in the separate receiver contract.
+No local lender return or copied disposition can prove any of those edges.
+
+After Main returns this implementation supplies no new cleanup frame or runtime
+operation permission. An outstanding lender remains retained until the real
+module cleanup operation and its actual Source/Native frame are integrated.
+Known id/thread, a replacement Main, callback success or an expired Setup guard
+cannot issue that authority. Missing physical joins fail closed without a
+second acquire, fabricated return or retry of a consumed destructor.
+
+Prebirth and qualification
+-------------------------
+
+The complete pending journal and its exclusive 1072-byte observation scratch
+are inline in the actual Source singleton and included by the real Source
+fixed-floor getter before birth. No preinit scratch, dynamic allocator or
+new protocol backing object is inferred as payment. Existing receiver/session
+parents retain the actual mapping, aliases and cleanup; their inventories
+remain distinct from this local child. Exact source-built complete-layout
+measurements against exact signed receiver base
+``6f597003260a33822b0226061e0c3eeb0ae695f6`` give Source 233208 bytes
+(previously 231944), a 1264-byte increase in the real fixed floor. The pending
+journal is 1264 bytes, including its 1072-byte scratch at offset 192; the journal
+starts at Source offset 12912. Member 696, service 256, receiver 1768, recipient
+3248, session 15912 and purpose storage 16024 bytes remain unchanged. No new
+Native dispatcher storage is introduced. These are process-private LP64 facts,
+not a public wire edition or evidence that a selected payer has issued them.
+A later union with other custody histories requires a new complete measurement.
+
+Actual configured Source, Native and x86/AArch64 preexec object compilation and
+literal causal controls establish only their stated component scope. Local
+geometry, immutable-byte and physical field-move leaves are not accepting owner
+fixtures. The genuine paid module constructor/Core operation, successful pending
+lender acquisition, enrolled module callbacks, deferred cleanup, RR/CPU/read
+children and class-one outcome remain unexecuted until their actual producers
+and payers join. The frozen receiver reconstruction remains unchanged.
+
+The configured object cohort has four actual objects (Source, Native, x86 and
+AArch64 preexec), compiled with the source-built configured compiler and GLib,
+at most two compilers concurrently, with 1536 observed inputs unchanged across
+the cohort. The literal preinit body passes 33 cases; its pending-copy reciprocal
+aborts if unexpectedly reached, since that fixture cannot own Source scratch.
+The legacy purpose extraction is byte-identical to the signed receiver body.
+The new controls rebuild 28 independent omissions covering span geometry,
+same-callback retry exclusion, local field consumption, complete immutable bytes
+and all independent refusing post cuts. Their positive spans and moves are local
+physical leaves, not a canonical Runtime, recipient or Original. The prior 109
+receiver omissions and separate capacity restriction also pass in this layout.
+
+The historical receiver extractor recorded one stale test hash. Independent
+comparison of all 266 signed extractor inputs reproduced the mismatch solely
+by adding back one trailing space on line 157 of the recipient-leaf test. The
+signed source and its manifests remain untouched. This checkpoint binds the
+actual signed test bytes and then the new production bytes; no historical test
