+Pending Quantum offer selection
+===============================
+
+This process-private selector supplies branch dispatch before the ordinary
+control callback attempts the nominal pending-command lender. It supplies no
+operation, Original, subscription membership, child, timer, event notification
+or ticket transition. A successful hint expires as an observation: a later
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_command_lend_v1`` independently checks
+and acquires the actual current recipient/cohort. The v6 receiver/Entry tables
+and v2--v5 interfaces are unchanged.
+
+Interface and owner
+-------------------
+
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_pending_offer_select_v1(member, version, bytes,
+out)`` accepts version 1 and the exact 32-byte, eight-byte-aligned
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_pending_offer_selection_v1``. Its fields are two u32
+version/size words, u32 state, zero u32 reserved, u64 publication sequence and
+u64 ticket serial. State 1 selects an observed immutable class-one Issued offer
+for dispatch. State 0 reports a transient observed no-offer cut; its sequence
+and serial are zero. A refusal leaves output untouched. Neither state grants
+permission, guarantees a later lend or certifies completed work.
+
+The Native adapter supplies its actual canonical Main/control ticket fields.
+Source authenticates the registered member, transferred service Runtime,
+installed publisher lender and actually entered callback frame. The charged
+Source root contains one exclusive observation journal. Exact output geometry
+is checked against the complete Runtime, Source, preexec and mapped session
+journals, including the canonical pending lender holder/serial fields, before
+any caller output changes. Busy observation excludes member/service/root
+retirement and recipient preparation/lend. It creates no new physical child;
+the actual calling Main retains its parent Runtime throughout this local read.
+
+The journal binds canonical addresses, process, thread, nonwrapping local
+serial and the same Main/control serials. Source and Native observations run
+outside the Source registry mutex. The preexec reciprocal accepts only that
+exact canonical journal and installed session; this is not an arbitrary
+mapped-buffer public reader.
+
+Bounded observation and return
+------------------------------
+
+One observation loads publication sequence and ticket, refuses an odd
+publication sequence, then copies all 512 naturally aligned atomic words of
+the actual 4096-byte session region once. It performs no retry. Literal public
+codecs validate immutable header and state-specific records. Header identity
+must corroborate the actual retained purpose/session. The final reserved span
+2816..4095 remains zero. The independent final cut rereads every copied word
+and the original sequence/ticket, including after a refused decode; an early
+odd read still gets the final sequence/ticket cut. Failed parent identity
+prevents further mapping access.
+
+An Issued offer requires a clean complete cohort, class-one primary,
+positive one-unit required inventory with no completed required work,
+permission phase 1 and the actual purpose account/process/capability/
+reservation correlation. Those checks classify bytes under existing service
+custody; they do not issue that operation. Acquired, ReturnRequested,
+Consumed and Withdrawn phases refuse. Busy, malformed, stale or refused
+observations never become absence.
+
+An empty mutable span reports no-offer only when the actual session has no
+recipient acquisition history or live recipient debt. Closed bytes report
+no-offer only with the actual retained recipient's acquired/returned/
+consumed/closed journal, closed row-view inventory, once-only return facts,
+matching immutable publication and return words, and actual cached terminal
+consumption. A syntactically valid Closed vector without that journal refuses.
+
+The local read records attempted, entered, physically returned and consumed
+separately. Independent Native, Source, installed-session and final statuses
+remain separate from first refusal. Local return uses physical identity,
+without requiring a successful semantic post. A returned local read may be
+consumed after a negative post, but publishes no usable selection. An entered
+read without a known physical return or a failed identity retains busy debt;
+there is no retry destructor or later cleanup authority inferred from Main
+identity. A second local return is refused. Neither reader consumption nor a
+Closed ticket establishes producer membership or semantic progress.
+
+Actual layout and evidence scope
+--------------------------------
+
+The exact signed baseline is
+``03734f44ee50d2cfc76169b0ad5d69b9be245afe`` (tree
+``6a7bbc0353ea3b26b7732dc0fb5cae34bd9f9f81``). Its Source root is 233208
+bytes. The configured layout with this reader is 238600 bytes: +5392 in the
+actual Source fixed floor, which already begins with ``sizeof(startup_source)``
+before preexec births. The journal starts at Source offset 14176 and contains
+5288-byte observation storage at offset 104, including the full 4096-byte
+atomic word copy and complete decoded views. All these layouts align to eight
+bytes. The public selection is 32 bytes. No dynamic allocator or inferred
+capacity payer is added.
+
+The existing 1264-byte pending lender, 696-byte member, 256-byte module
+service, 1768-byte receiver, 3248-byte preexec recipient, 15912-byte session
+and 16024-byte session storage purpose remain unchanged relative to that
+baseline. This is branch-local geometry, not a measurement of a later union
+with independent Runtime/construction changes. Every complete union must
+remeasure its actual Source root/floor before birth.
+
+Configured production checks compile actual Source, Native and both x86_64
+and AArch64 preexec objects using their source-built compiler/GLib inputs.
+The literal preinit tests exercise local mutable-span copy/final/decode leaves,
+including positive Issued and empty byte vectors, and refuse bare Closed
+bytes. They never enter a canonical paid Source/session/Main constructor.
+Separately rebuilt omissions retain unchanged assertions. A separate literal
+Source test exercises local return facts and independent posts whose every
+owner dependency refuses; it accepts no owner or Original.
+
+Genuine installed paid Source/member/session selector invocation, the actual
+external module pending constructor and retained Quantum Original remain
+unexecuted. RR/CPU admission remains ENOTSUP. No selected activation,
+producer-operation membership, semantic outcome or completed work-unit
+publication is qualified by these component checks.
