@@ -0,0 +1,633 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+
+Subscription lender construction dependencies
+============================================
+
+This describes the actual preexec storage and preparation-only session
+constructor, plus the still-missing producer/member joins. It does not advertise
+subscription support. The proposed public
+region and operation transitions are in ``crucible-publisher-subscription.rst``.
+
+Existing actual entry and receipt
+--------------------------------
+
+``preexec_setup_entry`` is the sole selected executable preinit parser. Setup 5
+is exactly 61 bytes with five/six SCM roles; the existing CRUCSUP8/schema 8 sealed
+purpose plan has a 40-byte header, optional 128-byte workspace, 128-byte startup
+record and the process-purpose record. None contains a subscription role.
+The installed module later owns its same existing stream/parser; introducing a
+second receiver or duplicating a live Setup receive cannot establish custody.
+
+The actual entry validates its retained peer and plan, then calls
+``preexec_setup_fixed_owner_retain``. That function executes the existing
+``preexec_setup_provisional_native(sizeof(*owner))`` reservation and records the
+successful exact charge before returning. A numerical prefix or unused local
+capacity cannot fill that receipt. Subsequent page-size, Original, real family
+assignment, aliases, limits, cgroup, credentials and artifact checks remain in
+their original order.
+
+After the actual contract observation, and before the RAM/standing/workspace
+constructors and Source publication, ``preexec_publisher_storage_construct``
+retains its canonical inline storage purpose. It requires that actual debit,
+the singleton, retained same Source assignment/family, initialized incarnation,
+artifact and process/thread. It records first and an independently executed
+Original post separately, retaining the receipt after either failure. The
+existing ``qemu_crucible_preexec_purpose_check_v3`` requires this same receipt
+before permitting Source publication or later purpose borrowing. There is no
+public storage constructor accepting arbitrary identity, extent or mapping.
+
+The storage constructor itself creates no aliases, mapping, session borrower or
+operation debt. The matched Setup 6 branch described below subsequently calls
+the real session constructor under this same canonical owner. Its journals are
+inside the already retained singleton, with no separate heap object or inferred
+dynamic payer. Setup 5 and Hello 8 keep their exact framing and roster. Selected
+preinit still terminates unavailable.
+
+Measured storage
+----------------
+
+The earlier storage prerequisite grew the actual configured LP64 preexec
+singleton from 185464 to 188880 bytes. This matched receiver checkpoint grows it
+to 189424 bytes (another 544 bytes), alignment 8. The receiver-service lender
+checkpoint grows it to 189480 bytes (another 56 bytes). Its canonical storage
+purpose is now 3520 bytes, containing a 3408-byte session journal. Each of its three alias journals
+is 176 bytes; the mapping journal is 48 bytes. The exclusive atomic-copy scratch
+is exactly 1536 bytes, followed by distinct decoded header/publication/return/
+terminal views. The new decoded purpose view is 152 bytes and the complete decoded plan is
+5096 bytes. The complete landing arrays are frame125, descriptors36 and
+ancillary56 bytes. The fixed-owner debit uses the complete 189480-byte layout, including all
+padding, before journal/session initialization and metadata/artifact effects.
+Initial SCM alias birth still requires the externally paid once carrier and
+its already enforced kernel landing ceiling; this later debit cannot issue
+that earlier entitlement. These are factual layout observations,
+not public wire layouts or authority.
+
+The real provisional floor consumes the enlarged ``sizeof(*owner)`` before any
+metadata/artifact effects. The actual existing 96-byte CRUCSTC2 constructor
+layout getter reports this same full extent at offset 80; its real standing
+constructor checks it. The literal unit reads that actual getter and complete
+owning layout. The Source native-prefix publication subsequently carries the
+actual retained debit; no Source layout is enlarged or separately charged.
+
+The three alias journals separate received, close-attempted, physical
+return, uncertainty and first/post/return status. The mapping journal separates
+actual acquisition, DONTFORK, unmap attempt and physical return. The session
+journal reserves its independent cleanup holder, operation count, nonwrapping
+local serial and exclusive snapshot state. None is initialized as successful
+because its storage was paid. The matched constructor performs actual map and
+alias custody; there remains no CAS, operation snapshot, event dispatch or
+module session borrowing. The receiver-service lender described below now
+retains its distinct Source and command-member tails; it still supplies no
+producer operation membership or module parser capability.
+
+Exact missing constructor contract
+----------------------------------
+
+The session constructor is an internal operation on this exact retained
+preexec singleton, called by its existing once-consumed entry. It must not take
+an arbitrary mapping or decoded header as issuer. Before any subscription
+alias/map birth, the following paired input must genuinely exist:
+
+* Setup 6 has the proposed exact 125-byte frame and eight/nine ordered SCM roles
+  from the same real peer/endpoint/family. Older Setup 5 remains exact. Actual
+  receive retains every received alias before any validation or fallible post;
+  malformed and truncated rosters keep their real physical acquisition debt.
+* A new matched sealed-purpose-plan edition binds the subscription roles,
+  actual producer session/lender generation, Source capability/reservation,
+  process/account incarnations and independent session-service payer. The
+  existing plan 8 supplies no such role. Its extension must be defined and
+  joined to the producer's real role constructors; no record assembled
+  from fstat, header equality or spare native capacity substitutes for them.
+* Its real purpose joins the actual kernel aliases, event objects, mapping
+  controls, runtime/parser/module cleanup tail and rounded page backing. The
+  parent Original and independent session-service cleanup holder are retained
+  separately from operation memberships. Their concrete extents/counts must
+  be reserved before birth, without charging the same backing twice.
+
+Under that same owner the constructor checks exact role/length/seal/access
+geometry, inherited limits and real page size; records each actual alias before
+post; reserves the actual rounded mapping backing; performs the actual writable
+shared mmap and DONTFORK; then records each result before independently observing
+the same Original. Partial failure keeps canonical journals and real aliases.
+An uncertain close/unmap is never repeated or converted into physical return.
+The storage receipt alone permits none of those effects.
+
+Only that genuine session may then lend aligned lock-free atomic words. Its
+actual retained canonical journal must own every bounded before/data/after
+snapshot and exact-ticket CAS. A busy/changed observation refuses without an
+internal retry. Acquired operations increment real nonwrapping debt before
+exposing a result, retain genuine producer-issued memberships, and join the
+separate terminal-consumed and locally-closed facts. Decoding or CAS alone
+constructs neither those memberships nor a semantic Original.
+
+Matched constructor edition
+---------------------------
+
+The new branch uses Setup 6, tag ``0x16``, exactly 120 payload bytes and a
+125-byte length/tag/payload frame. Setup 5 remains exactly as above. Payload
+bytes 0..55 retain their existing meanings. The extension is BEu64 lender
+generation at 56, region length at 64 (4096), device at 72, inode at 80,
+producer-to-receiver event token at 88 and receiver-to-producer event token at
+96; BEu32 region schema at 104 (1), flags at 108 (1), and zero bytes 112..119.
+All generations and event tokens are in 1..UINT64_MAX-1. The two event tokens
+must differ. Device/inode are exact kernel witnesses, with no guessed device
+or nonzero-inode requirement. Workspace schema still determines presence.
+
+The existing five roles, and optional workspace sixth role, retain their exact
+order. The three new roles immediately follow: writable publisher region,
+producer-to-receiver eventfd and receiver-to-producer eventfd. Thus Setup 6 has
+exactly eight or nine descriptors. Receipt is still one nonblocking recvmsg by
+the existing once owner, with no late receiver. Its fixed ancillary landing
+storage and inherited descriptor ceiling cover the largest edition before
+receipt. Every received alias is retained before semantic validation.
+
+Plan 9 is ``CRUCSUP9``, schema 9, with a 48-byte big-endian header. Bytes 8..39
+have the same field meanings as plan 8, except header length is 48. BEu32 at 40
+is subscription record length 224; bytes 44..47 are zero. Its body is app,
+selectable, optional workspace, startup, process purpose, then subscription.
+The existing independent app/selectable and aggregate file caps are unchanged;
+all offsets are widened and checked before narrowing. The new decoded C views
+are process-private. Setup 5 requires plan 8;
+Setup 6 requires plan 9. The process-purpose record itself remains CRUCPUR8.
+
+The sealed subscription-purpose record is exactly 224 bytes. Integer fields
+are BEu64 except schema/length (BEu32). No native pointers cross this boundary.
+
+================= ====== =====================================================
+Field             Offset Required value or binding
+================= ====== =====================================================
+magic             0      eight bytes CRUCPSP1
+schema / length   8 / 12 1 / 224
+lender generation 16     1..UINT64_MAX-1, same Setup 6
+account generation 24    1..UINT64_MAX-1, same real Source account
+process generation 32    1..UINT64_MAX-1, same Source execution incarnation
+capability        40     32 bytes, actual containing capability
+reservation       72     32 bytes, actual Source reservation identity
+region device     104    same Setup and actual received region
+region inode      112    same Setup and actual received region
+region bytes      120    4096, same Setup and actual file length
+producer event    128    same Setup and actual eventfd token
+receiver event    136    same Setup and actual eventfd token, distinct from 128
+backing bytes     144    checked actual host-page rounding of 4096
+cleanup generation 152   exactly 1, issued by the once-only storage constructor
+native debit      160    exactly backing bytes; controls already in fixed owner
+alias inventory   168    exactly 3 received aliases, separate from inherited FDs
+file inventory    176    exactly 4096 existing producer file bytes
+flags             184    exactly 1 (independent preexec cleanup holder)
+reserved          192    32 zero bytes
+================= ====== =====================================================
+
+The actual canonical storage constructor issues cleanup generation 1 only once
+after its real fixed-owner debit and Source binding. There is no reset/reuse
+constructor; a decoded generation cannot initialize or advance that identity.
+
+The purpose record is not a constructor. Only the actual once owner, retained
+Main peer, entered installing Original, authentic family Source assignment,
+actual kernel contract and artifact may reach the session constructor. Before
+mmap, it executes the existing Source provisional-native debit for the rounded
+backing and records its exact successful receipt. The enlarged actual fixed
+owner separately pays all journals and scratch before their initialization.
+This mapping reservation does not create a second file/page object: producer
+file backing remains a separate physical inventory. The receiver conservatively
+reserves the rounded mapping span inside its real local share; page-table and
+kernel containment still require its actual process contract. The same actual
+contract contains the extra descriptor landing and writable file inventory; these are not a new bank issued by decoded counts. The producer
+must have paid for file/eventfd creation, queued SCM references and overlapping
+aliases before sending. Those producer operations are not implemented here.
+
+The constructor's cleanup holder is an actual field in the paid preexec storage,
+pointing to its canonical session. It belongs to the retained Source assignment
+and is independent of all operation membership. It is installed before mapping
+or callbacks and is never transferred to an unretained runtime. No operation
