+Pending Quantum/Advance handoff proposal
+=======================================
+
+Status and existing boundary
+----------------------------
+
+This is an unimplemented process-private SDK proposal for paired review. It
+advertises no capability and changes no public socket/shared-memory bytes.
+``qemu_crucible_source_quantum_cpu_admit_v1()`` must retain its ENOTSUP result
+until the actual paired producer and every dependency below exist. The
+Setup6 service mapping, its bounded observations, and a decoded CRUCQCM1 command
+are physical service/syntax dependencies; none issues an operation membership.
+
+The existing member constructor is
+``qemu_plugin_crucible_startup_source_command_member_create_v5()`` in
+``include/plugins/qemu-plugin.h`` and
+``plugins/crucible-command-membership.inc.h``. It binds reader/writer, payload
+claim/release, payload lifetime acquire/release and four fingerprint-action
+callbacks to the same completed child, independent Bridge, registered component,
+assigned mapping/slot and paid Runtime. Its movable member projection is
+transferred with ``...command_member_transfer_v1()`` to an exact Runtime field.
+Negative creation/transfer posts retain the actual born or moved custody.
+
+The v5 ``QemuCrucibleModuleFingerprintAction`` remains synchronous with Main
+CALLING. ``qemu_crucible_ram_fingerprint_action_baseline_v1()`` chooses only the
+actual initialization/update fingerprint class. No v2-v5 signature or class
+selection changes. An Advance cannot use the fingerprint action field, stretch
+CALLING, retag a Preparation, or inherit a stopped construction CPU permission.
+
+Proposed C contract
+-------------------
+
+The following declarations define the proposed matched edition. The working
+SDK addition remains unavailable for operation admission until its genuine
+producer and receiver counterparts join. All objects are true opaque C tags, confined to the QEMU process.
+No native object, address or callback table crosses the process protocol.
+
