+
+The v6 constructor would require every existing v5 callback and every new
+callback. It would validate exact version/size, complete pointer extents and
+callback table disjointness before mutation, then copy the table by value into
+the actually charged nominal member. It would retain no caller table pointer.
+The existing create/transfer post and failed-birth rules apply unchanged.
+An older member has no Advance producer; absence does not select a fallback
+Quantum issuer. A module must implement the actual pending-Advance owner before
+registering v6; a successful callback stub is not a permitted counterpart.
+
+The disposition is output scratch in the canonical Source journal, exclusively
+held during one callback. Source sets version/size and sentinel facts before
+entry. Only exact 0/1 physical facts are canonical. The callback return code,
+first status and post status are independent signed outcomes (zero or negative).
+The publication fields are monotonic factual receipts from the actual entered
+publication producer: a nonzero, nonwrapping work-unit serial accompanies exactly
+one published unit; before publication both are zero. They corroborate the held
+outcome/producer and cannot create it. Returned bits likewise require actual
+field/serial consumption. Original returns only after every actually born
+Advance returned, or after that same Enter's authenticated Advance-no-birth
+edge. In the latter partial-move case ``original_returned=1`` may coexist with
+``advance_returned=0``; the absent Advance must never receive a fabricated
+physical-return bit.
+None of these receipts alone proves ownership or complete work. Source retains its own first,
+validation, independent post, identity and physical facts separately, rather than
+reusing these module fields as Source authority.
+
+Canonical birth and immutable command
+-------------------------------------
+
+Source would add one distinct prepaid Advance journal with fixed fields
+``module_original``, ``module_original_serial``, ``module_advance`` and
+``module_advance_serial``. Every callback receives those exact four addresses;
+the physical Original move and actual Advance birth retain their addresses
+and nonwrapping serials. No movable caller
+projection, reconstructed module pointer or arbitrary Runtime address substitutes
+for those fields. Module Current and Return authenticate both original nominal
+holders, their original serials and their same actual child relationship.
+
+``enter`` runs only from the actual assigned command's Main CALLING boundary,
+using the exact retained asynchronous command, membership and cleanup fields.
+The actual component/member and separate asynchronous recipient/command borrower
+must already be retained. The existing synchronous Ready/delivery/payload chain
+remains separate: its Native action predicate requires ``main_borrow`` and must
+not be reused to authenticate an asynchronous command. The new physical
+Main/callback observation authenticates the actual canonical CONTROL frame and
+entered registered callback, with QOM/allocation/Runtime custody, even when the
+synchronous payload borrower is absent. That observation grants no Original. The new receiver below supplies those
+canonical fields; fingerprint payload/borrow callbacks are not repurposed. Source also
+retains the actual publisher operation membership, immutable command borrower,
+Runtime/child/Bridge and independent cleanup holder before invoking the producer.
+If any of these genuinely missing dependencies is known absent, it refuses
+before invoking ``enter`` or creating a physical operation child.
+
+The actual module must resolve the pending semantic command through its retained
+immutable command owner, not from a caller's decoded command. Acquisition retains the one preexisting entered class-one Quantum Original
+inside its true immutable command owner. Enter moves that same actual Original
+from the command owner's canonical field to Source's exact ``module_original``
+and serial fields; it creates only the true Advance child. It records
+``original_moved=1`` immediately after the physical move, before any fallible
+post or Advance birth. The old module field becomes NULL/zero and the command
+retains the reverse destination addresses and incarnation. No second Original
+is constructed or issued. Failed Advance birth or a negative post retains that
+moved Original, its exact Source holder and all cleanup parents. The Original/Advance owns the immutable command incarnation and
+producer memberships through terminal consumption. A pending preparation/reset
+branch must return authenticated absence, never convert its operation class.
+
+``entry`` is an opaque observation of the real Native Main producer and exact
+Source handoff, valid only during this invocation. It binds the actual current
+Main ticket, assigned command owner, retained operation membership, canonical
+member, process/thread and nonwrapping serial. It is not permission minted by
+this callback. Its Source implementation must first authenticate those existing
+parents; a byte-valid command cannot construct it. The existing older standing
+subscription and Setup6 atomic session are distinct protocols: their values
+must not be combined into a synthetic producer membership. In particular,
+``QemuCruciblePublisherActionLoan`` currently requires a fingerprint
+``QemuCrucibleActionOriginal`` and Main CALLING; it is not the asynchronous
+membership borrower proposed here. The real paired producer must supply that
+separate retained operation loan before this entry can become accepting.
+
+The command binding includes the actual publication identity and stable even,
+nonzero, nonwrapping scheduler generation; initial raw icount and maximum raw
+icount; explicit stop mode; effective logical and native ceilings; command
+frontier; and next-idle target when required by the stop mode. The existing
+CRUCQCM1 geometry/canonical rules remain the wire syntax. Copies in the Source
+journal serve comparison and budgeting only. Every permission cut authenticates
+the same retained command publisher/Original; equality of these copies does not
+renew or issue that relationship. Raw retired-instruction counts (initial and
+maximum), scheduler logical ticks (including the actual idle offset), and native
+absolute monotonic deadline nanoseconds are three different domains. Native
+ceiling presence comes from the retained Original/cohort clock contract:
+``native_ceiling_present=0`` denotes deliberate absence; a present zero is expiry,
+never absence. The numeric native field alone encodes neither permission nor
+presence, and no logical/raw multiplication produces that deadline. The raw
+ceiling separately needs the real scheduler calibration and live device/idle
+constraints. CRUCQCM1 bytes remain unchanged; the presence observation is a
+process-private corroboration of the actual clock owner. A bounded
+busy/odd/changed observation refuses;
+there is no retry loop or per-Quantum socket exchange.
+
+``known_absent=1`` is accepted only with negative status, NULL/zero outputs and
+an independently authenticated no-birth return of this entered callback,
+including ``original_moved=0``. A born
+output is saved before evaluating signed status or independent post. Partial,
+contradictory or uncertain outputs retain all parents and exact fields; they
+cannot be overwritten on a later command. There is no second issuer attempt.
+The contract needs a real module partial-birth cleanup implementation, using its
+retained cleanup owner, before any constructor can become accepting.
+
+Handoff while Main is still CALLING
+----------------------------------
+
+After the Original move and any attempted Advance birth, Source independently observes the same actual Original,
+command membership and entered Main holder. ``handoff_post`` then records the
+module's independent same-Original post before Main CALLING ends. Source runs
+its independent final observation even after a negative module result, saving
+every status without returning the child from status alone.
+
+A successful handoff retains the asynchronous journal, immutable command and
+Original independently from the short Main callback frame. It increments real
+member/Runtime/producer operation debts before the actual Main command borrower can
+return. The module must retain the actual immutable semantic command it needs;
+the Main borrower is physically returned, not silently kept CALLING. The new
+journal never points at the soon-dead Main stack ticket as its current issuer.
+Main QOM/registration custody returns normally only after its own actual child
+return; it does not return or activate the Advance.
+
+A failed post still leaves the born Advance/Original and all parents retained.
+Cleanup uses its genuine independent cleanup operation, not expired Main/Setup
+permission. That operation must exist before entering any fallible, waiting or
+callback cleanup work. Identity-only physical consumption is insufficient to
+issue a new cleanup work interval.
+
+RR CPU/read entry and return
+----------------------------
+
+The current real producer is ``rr_quantum_cpu_acquire()``. It pins the actual
+CPU QOM instance, stores the canonical stack holder in the inline
+``QemuCrucibleQuantumCpuExecution`` and calls
+``qemu_crucible_source_quantum_cpu_admit_v1()`` before BQL unlock. Source already
+resolves the genuine QOM allocation receipt and allocation generation there.
+
+The eventual accepting branch must additionally retain the handed-off Advance,
+actual same Original/command, CPU generation and allocation receipt, and a typed
+Native RR child before permission is granted. ``QemuCrucibleSourceAdvanceUse``
+authenticates that exact entered RR holder/thread/serial and its same retained
+Original; its address alone grants nothing. A module Current callback under this
+use must support this authenticated RR actor without requiring expired Main
+CALLING or widening Main current to a process/thread/id comparison.
+
+The same typed use must retain any actual runtime register borrower/read children
+and their architecture effect dependencies. Construction-time read permission
+cannot be reused. APIC timer storage/callback custody, VAPIC AddressSpace effects,
+ARM raw callbacks, allocator/handler users and actual output publications retain
+their separate owners. Missing dependencies keep CPU admission refused.
+
+Each current/entry callback saves first and module post independently, then
+Source performs its own same-Original/command/holder final observation on every
+outcome. No callback runs under the Source ledger or Native registration mutex.
+Only after these cuts may RR unlock BQL and enter ``tcg_cpu_exec()``.
+``cpu_exec_start/end`` and longjmp cleanup revoke permission separately from
+physical execution end and actual child return. A longjmp continuation must
+return to RR or genuinely reauthenticate under this same Original; it cannot
+reacquire permission from the copied tuple. Real execution/read children return
+before the RR physical child, QOM pin and allocation references can return.
+
+Outcome publication and final physical disposition
+-------------------------------------------------
+
+The proposed ``QemuCrucibleNativeAdvanceOutcome`` is another opaque retained
+producer observation, not a caller-populated result struct. RR may create it
+only after the real retired ceiling, or authenticated next-idle producer
+completion, under the same actual scheduler command and Original. Actual final
+icount must be observed and all required children returned. It cannot be created
+from callback count, instruction count alone, ACK, loop iteration or a supplied
+next-idle generation. External restore uses its separate operation boundary.
+
+``publish`` enters the actual module producer's once-only work-unit publication
+with the authentic outcome and held Advance use. Source saves actual attempted,
+published, consumed and returned facts separately from first/post and performs
+its independent post even on refusal. A genuine work unit completes exactly once
+at actual publication; an interrupted or uncertain publication retains debt and
+forbids a second attempt. Outcome publication and physical protocol terminal
+consumption are distinct, including after a negative final post.
+
+``return_child`` can enter only after all real execution/read/handler children,
+entered uses and publication effects returned, with independently held module
+cleanup authority. Its actual destructor must consume any born Advance before Original,
+null each actually consumed canonical field and zero its serial, then report the corresponding
+physical returned bits. A negative status can accompany physical consumption;
+Source records consumption and must never resurrect or release it again.
+Unknown disposition retains parents and blocks reentry. No automatic return
+retry or fresh cleanup issuer is supplied by this ABI.
+
+Parent order is children/uses -> actual work-unit publication -> actual local
+Advance return -> actual local Original return -> producer terminal consumption
+-> operation membership/command release -> member/component/Runtime/session
+cleanup. Session protocol-service and independent module cleanup holders may
+outlive operation membership for the final post and last unref; they must not be
+counted as work children whose return waits on their own terminal consumption.
+Every independent physical attempt and debit is recorded once before effect.
+
+Recipient inventory and physical return
+--------------------------------------
+
+The seven ``PublisherReturn.physical_child_mask`` bits remain factual reports,
+not a born mask or an authorization predicate. Each bit means its corresponding
+category contained an actually entered child whose physical return is proved.
+An unset bit does not authenticate absence. Source must never initialize this
+mask to all returned, derive it from signed success, or use its copied value to
+close a debt.
+
+The canonical Native recipient owns the complete inventory before each child
+effect. Each category retains separate constructor-attempted, born, entered,
+authenticated-not-entered/no-birth, return-attempted, physically-returned and
+uncertain facts, with its actual canonical holder/serial and first/post. The
+constructor or real producer records those facts; neither the return serializer
+nor a module disposition creates them. A genuinely entered callback that returns
+without child birth supplies only its actual callback-return/no-birth edge.
+The independent same-Original post runs even on that branch. Once-only attempted
+and consumed facts survive negative post and prohibit another release.
+
+A complete executable class-one handoff requires the actual semantic
+Original/Advance callback category (bit 0), RR execution/end/cleanup category
+(3), CPU/QOM category (4), and single outcome publication category (6). Stop mode
+2 additionally retains the actual next-idle subscription/callback category (5)
+before permitting its completion path. Material/worker (1) and read/effect (2)
+are additional required categories whenever their real constructors enter them;
+a capacity or an unused hook cannot authenticate absence. A healthy work unit
+cannot bypass any mandatory producer. Partial acquisition or failed birth may
+return physical custody with no outcome, only after every born child returned
+and each never-entered required branch has an authenticated no-entry fact from
+that exact constructor/producer. Unknown or interrupted disposition retains the
+recipient, command, memberships and cleanup owner.
+
+The actual registered ``advance.return_child`` is the semantic local-return
+producer: it consumes the exact Advance before the moved Original under the
+independently entered cleanup use. Source records physical callback return
+separately, retains all independent post failures, and checks its entire
+constructor inventory rather than only the callback's bits. Only the canonical
+Source recipient terminal producer, entered through that retained journal and
+its actual cleanup operation, may serialize a return and CAS its exact Acquired
+ticket to ReturnRequested. No public mask-writing API substitutes for that
+registered producer.
+
+A separately bounded no-birth tail is possible only when the actual Source
+journal retained its independent session and Runtime cleanup parents before
+the recipient acquire CAS. The same entered acquire frame must independently
+authenticate every module output as never entered and absent; a negative status
+and null outputs alone are insufficient. Source preserves first and independent
+post separately and publishes zero completed units. This factual tail may only
+publish the bounded return record and compare-exchange its exact Acquired ticket
+to ReturnRequested. It performs no callback, wait, notification syscall, new
+Original or Setup fallback. The journal and session remain retained through
+actual producer consumption. Any moved Original, entered constructor, partial
+output or uncertain birth retains the genuine module cleanup path. No branch
+attempts acquisition a second time.
+
+The peer's actual recipient was retained before its offer on the same
+constructor-authenticated installed session. ReturnRequested is the paired
+receiver's physical return edge under that contract. The peer independently
+checks its own immutable command/recipient incarnation and performs its actual
+lender and command destruction, retaining first/post and consumption facts,
+before publishing terminal consumption. An all-set mask, decoded record, ACK or
+matching identifiers cannot supply that destruction. This protocol carries no
+Native pointers or per-Quantum socket proof. Module membership, command and
+cleanup tail returns follow actual producer consumption; the session/service
+pins needed to observe that consumption are not work children awaiting their
+own destruction.
+
+Prebirth payment and layout requirements
+---------------------------------------
+
+On the frozen a613 source cohort, actual measured Source is 230032 bytes, its
+module-service journal is 248 bytes, callback owner is 192 bytes, and the Native
+component is 104 bytes. Its physical return frame is 56 bytes; watcher and serial
+make the real Native storage getter 232 bytes. These measurements are not payer
+or owner authority. Other signed layout histories require composition and new
+measurements, not reuse of this cohort's complete-object qualification.
+
+Before any new births, ``sizeof(startup_source)`` must include the distinct
+Advance journal, exact fields/serials, all first/post/identity/physical receipts,
+exclusive callback scratch, bounded command copies and outcome journal. The
+member must include the copied callback table and actual Advance debt; callback
+owner, command receive/delivery and retained operation publisher must include the
+specific parent debts they enforce. CPUState's actual inline RR body must price
+any new CPU/read child or witness fields. Each real Native producer/cleanup frame
+must join its actual static storage observer. No extra unpriced TLS singleton,
+heap vector, inferred payer or capacity-based object birth is allowed.
+
+The actual fixed floor is
+``qemu_crucible_startup_source_fixed_control_extent()``: complete Source plus its
+checked receiving, Stop, construction, wake, fingerprint, Park, RAM and descriptor
+storage getters. Its real provisional preexec reservation and metadata partition
+must retain the enlarged result before birth. Implementation must measure every
+complete type and observer with matching configured objects, checked addition,
+and independent omitted-span controls; this proposal assigns no invented total.
+
+The external Runtime layout also changes: it needs genuine owned Original,
+Advance and immutable-command state, cleanup holders, exact canonical-field
+bindings, publication/terminal journals and callback dispatch support for the
+actual RR actor. Those bytes must appear in the producer's actual allocation
+requests, layout section, placement/destruction and corresponding-source build.
+The module's independently retained operation payer must cover runtime,
+allocator/handler/read-effect work; existing service custody pays none of these
+operations. The current module/service transfer is a parent lifetime prerequisite,
+not this payer or operation admission.
+
+Acceptance required before an accepting implementation
+------------------------------------------------------
+
+A genuine positive must use the real paid module Runtime and registered v6
+member, actual assigned command and producer membership, real entered class-one
+Original, immutable command and same Main entry. It must demonstrate durable
+birth before Main return, real RR CPU QOM/allocation and read-effect children,
+permission revocation plus actual execution/cleanup return, exact ceiling and
+next-idle completion variants, one actual publication and all physical terminal
+returns. A matching full-layout executable and actual counterpart are required;
+a local nominal journal or successful provider stub cannot replace this case.
+
+Independent causal omissions must cover wrong Main/member/assigned command,
+wrong process/thread/canonical field/nonwrapping serial, preparation/reset,
+missing Original/payer/producer member, partial birth and negative first/post,
+odd/changed/withdrawn publication, changed stop/ceiling/next-idle command,
+QOM/allocation or CPU-generation mismatch, missing read/effect child return,
+longjmp continuation, callback first failure with independent post still run,
+uncertain publication, duplicate work-unit/return attempts, consumed-negative
+post, physical-return-before-child violations, parent retirement with retained
+debt, and overflow/alias/short-capacity refusal before mutation. These cases test
+actual bodies and real producer/destructor branches where present, and label
+any component-only leaf separately. Until the paired semantic producer exists,
+all genuine positive cases remain unexecuted and ENOKEY/ENOTSUP remains intact.
+
