+``module_command_serial``, ``module_membership``, ``module_membership_serial``,
+``module_cleanup`` and ``module_cleanup_serial`` inside the actual prepaid Source
+receiver journal. Their addresses never move. The module retains those exact
+addresses and nonwrapping local serials in its true objects. It must retain its
+actual cleanup operation before creating a fallible partial command/membership
+birth. It must retain the actual immutable pending command, its true entered
+Quantum Original and real host operation-publisher membership before publishing
+the corresponding output fields. Their backing is that retained ownership,
+never the observation structs below. Source saves every born output before
+validation and independently posts the real Source membership on every callback
+outcome. Acquisition known absence needs a negative, all NULL/zero outputs, no attempted or
+returned facts and a genuinely returned acquisition callback. Partial outputs
+retain actual Source/module parents and prohibit replacement by a later command.
