+creation. ``cleanup_enter`` retains that genuinely entered operation's true
+opaque guard in the fixed ``module_cleanup_guard`` and
+``module_cleanup_guard_serial`` Source fields. It does not take a Source use.
+The module retains those exact addresses before output, even on negative post.
+``cleanup_current`` authenticates the actual entered guard and its retained
+cleanup owner without requiring any Source use. Only after that reciprocal
+observation may Source enter its paid cleanup use; its independent post runs on
+every outcome and a negative result retains the use's creation holder. Neither
+callback creates an operation or cleanup interval from a Source token. A Source frame or successful callback alone is
+insufficient. The reciprocal implementation must authenticate the real module
+cleanup owner/entered guard, exact Runtime, process/thread and nonwrapping guard
+incarnation before any fallible cleanup callback. If that actual issuer is not
+available, the Source child and all owners remain retained. Component-return's
+narrow physical service frame cannot supply this work authority.
+
+The return callbacks have distinct once-only attempt and physical-return
+facts. Membership return requires actual producer terminal consumption and all
+operation children returned. Command return follows membership return, keeping
+the immutable command until its final publisher observation. Cleanup return is
+last, after the command, Original/Advance, Source publication membership and all
+remaining session/post work that needs it. All actual cleanup work and Source
+cleanup uses must physically return before the factual tail is entered.
+``cleanup_guard_return`` then consumes only the exact already retained guard,
+nulling its field/serial; it may perform no new cleanup work, wait or callback.
+Its actual return and independent post are saved in the external Source journal.
+``cleanup_return`` requires that consumed guard fact, then consumes only the exact
+retained cleanup owner. The tail's current predicate checks its actual entered
+Native return frame, exact canonical Source journal, process/thread/serial,
+retained Runtime/registration/service tail pins and closed work/use debts. It
+reads guard and cleanup consumption from that external journal, never from a
+consumed object. The final callback's independent post likewise reads retained
+journals, not the freed guard or owner. No Original current check is required to
+consume an already retained physical tail; expired/negative Original evidence
+remains saved separately and grants no new work. No tail callback runs after its
+physical return or consumes either field twice.
+A negative result after any actual consumption saves that physical fact and
+cannot trigger another release. Unknown physical disposition retains its exact
+holder and independent parents. This order grants no publication from return
+bits and introduces no retry cleanup path.
+
+Exact copied observations
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+These structures are process-private numeric corroboration, never public wire
+layouts, ownership receipts or capability tokens. All methods take exact
+version/size and fresh caller-owned output backing; they validate complete
+extent/alignment/disjointness against every canonical journal, callback scratch
+and retained holder before mutation. All refusals preserve output. Observation
+copies are bounded and published only after independent before/after checks of
+the same actual nominal journal and entered producer. No observation method calls
+back into the module, recursively runs Current or creates an owner.
+
+.. code-block:: c
+
+    struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_binding_v1 {
+        uint64_t source_receiver_serial;
+        uint64_t source_publication_serial;
+        uint64_t command_sequence;
+        uint64_t loan_generation;
+        uint64_t ticket_serial;
+        uint64_t scheduler_generation;
+        uint64_t initial_raw_icount;
+        uint64_t max_advance_raw_icount;
+        uint64_t logical_tick_ceiling;
+        uint64_t native_ceiling_ns;
+        uint64_t command_frontier;
+        uint64_t next_idle_generation;
+        uint32_t stop_mode;
+        uint32_t native_ceiling_present; /* actual Original clock contract */
+        uint32_t reserved;             /* zero */
+        uint32_t reserved_tail;        /* zero */
+    };
+
+    struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_receiver_observation_v1 {
+        uint32_t schema_version;       /* 1 */
+        uint32_t struct_size;
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_binding_v1 binding;
+    };
+
+    struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_entry_observation_v1 {
+        uint32_t schema_version;       /* 1 */
+        uint32_t struct_size;
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_binding_v1 binding;
+        uint64_t source_entry_serial;
+        uint64_t main_invocation_serial;
+    };
+
+    struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_use_observation_v1 {
+        uint32_t schema_version;       /* 1 */
+        uint32_t struct_size;
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_binding_v1 binding;
+        uint64_t source_use_serial;
+        uint64_t rr_execution_serial;
+        uint64_t cpu_generation;
+        uint64_t allocation_generation;
+    };
+
+    struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_outcome_observation_v1 {
+        uint32_t schema_version;       /* 1 */
+        uint32_t struct_size;
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_binding_v1 binding;
+        uint64_t source_outcome_serial;
+        uint64_t final_raw_icount;
+        uint64_t completed_next_idle_generation;
+        uint32_t outcome;              /* 1 retired ceiling; 2 next-idle */
+        uint32_t reserved;             /* zero */
+    };
+
+    struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_cleanup_observation_v1 {
+        uint32_t schema_version;       /* 1 */
+        uint32_t struct_size;
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_binding_v1 binding;
+        uint64_t source_cleanup_use_serial;
+        uint64_t module_guard_serial;
+    };
+
+    struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_tail_observation_v1 {
+        uint32_t schema_version;       /* 1 */
+        uint32_t struct_size;
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_binding_v1 binding;
+        uint64_t source_tail_serial;
+        uint64_t consumed_guard_serial;
+        uint32_t guard_return_attempted;
+        uint32_t guard_returned;
+        uint32_t cleanup_return_attempted;
+        uint32_t cleanup_returned;
+        int32_t original_first_status;
+        int32_t original_post_status;
+    };
+
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_receiver_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourceAdvanceReceiver *receiver,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_receiver_observation_v1 *out);
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_command_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourceAdvanceCommandBorrow *borrow,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_receiver_observation_v1 *out);
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_entry_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourceAdvanceEntry *entry,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_entry_observation_v1 *out);
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_use_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourceAdvanceUse *use,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_use_observation_v1 *out);
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_outcome_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleNativeAdvanceOutcome *outcome,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_outcome_observation_v1 *out);
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_cleanup_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourceAdvanceCleanupUse *use,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_cleanup_observation_v1 *out);
+    int qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_tail_observe_v1(
+        QemuCrucibleSourceAdvanceCleanupTail *tail,
+        uint32_t version, size_t bytes,
+        struct qemu_plugin_crucible_advance_tail_observation_v1 *out);
+
+
+Receiver observation requires the exact canonical currently entered Native
+receiver, its same registered member/actual assigned command and genuine retained
+Source asynchronous publication membership. Command observation requires the
+exact entered current/borrow callback, same retained immutable command and that
+same real membership. Entry observation additionally requires the actual Main
+CALLING holder and same retained receiver/command incarnation. Use observation
+requires the actual canonical retained RR holder, actual entered use callback,
+same Original/Advance, CPU generation and live QOM/allocation receipt and their
+real child debts. Outcome observation requires the genuinely entered once-only
+publication callback and actual private RR ceiling/idle completion producer,
+with execution/read children physically returned. Every check binds canonical
+addresses before dereferencing nominated objects, the real process/thread,
+nonzero nonwrapping serial and the same before/after publication incarnation.
+Cleanup-use observation additionally authenticates the independently retained
+actual entered module guard, the exact cleanup-use frame and closed admission to
+unrelated work. Tail observation instead checks the retained external journal and
+its exact entered factual return callback. It never calls cleanup current or
+reads a consumed guard/owner. Its returned flags and saved statuses remain
+corroboration; the underlying frame authorizes only consuming that exact retained
+tail. Borrow lifetime is the actual entered callback; copied data grants no later
+use.
+
+The module independently authenticates its own immutable command, membership,
+entered Original and cleanup operation. An observation may corroborate that
+relationship but cannot supply a missing module owner or permit a different
+command to use the same Source token. Idle completion is authenticated through
+its actual Native producer; equality with the requested target generation is
+necessary corroboration, never its completion proof. Work-unit publication is
+still the actual module producer's single completed unit after this outcome.
+
+All receiver records, copied callback tables, exact pointer/serial fields,
+observation/disposition scratch, canonical entered frames and independent
+partial-birth/return receipts must reside in the actual charged Source/member,
+Native receiver or CPU layouts before birth. Source membership debts gate the
+real delivery/Ready/member/terminal/session parents; module cleanup is independent
+of operation work children. New complete-layout measurements and the actual
+checked fixed-floor/preexec reservation must include every added span. A table
+capacity, decoded geometry or this proposal supplies none of that payment.
+
+Working Native registration measurements
+---------------------------------------
+
+Against the retained a613 layout, the current two copied tables are 48 and 72
+bytes; the actual member is 688 bytes and Source is 230152 bytes, each enlarged
+by 120 bytes. Advance and receiver dispositions are each 56 bytes. The binding
+observation is 112 bytes, including explicit native-ceiling presence and two
+zero reserved words; it has no implicit trailing padding. These measurements
+cover the working registration scope, not the complete future recipient/frame
+journals or a payment claim. New complete-layout accounting must include those
+actual journals before their births. The genuine paid registration, recipient,
+Original, execution, cleanup and external counterpart positives remain
+unexecuted; literal callback-table tests invoke no producer.
