+Native sim control delivery
+===========================
+
+The ``crucible_sim_rr_control_delivery`` companion event is disabled by
+default. Enable it with ``--trace crucible_sim_rr_control_delivery`` or put
+that event name in the file passed to ``--trace events=<file>``. The existing
+``crucible_sim_rr_control_boundary`` event remains independently available.
+The log backend uses the normal QEMU log destination (``-D <file>``).
+
+The companion reports native request, acknowledgment and completion
+generations, the RR claim token, the current main-loop schedule token,
+deferred intent, RR execution state, numeric runstate and current RR vCPU
+owner and process ID. ``registered-enter`` immediately precedes the
+registered callback; ``registered-return`` immediately follows its return.
+``callback-enter``
+alone indicates entry to the native wrapper, which also checks that a CPU
+and callback are present. Native completion precedes the callback and does
+not establish that the callback acknowledged an external request.
+
+Fixed per-phase atomic diagnostic maxima deduplicate observations by native
+request generation and schedule sequence. The sequence distinguishes
+separate paused deliveries whose native generations remain equal. Repeated
+observations of unchanged ownership emit no further records. Concurrent
+claims can emit at most three records for the first ownership tuple and two
+for a subsequent tuple. Total output grows with distinct requests and
+schedules; no process-wide quota hides late requests. Fields are advisory
+snapshots rather than an atomic multi-field receipt. The cache resets on the
+first enabled native observation after a process ID change, so inherited
+parent maxima cannot hide early child delivery. Native transition call sites
+hold BQL; diagnostic fields use atomic accesses. No host clock is read,
+and diagnostic bookkeeping does not participate in admission or canonical
+state. These events establish native delivery only; callback behavior and
+physical fork or guest qualification require their own evidence.
+
 Trace backends
 ==============
 
