+/* Selected Crucible Source enumerates its realized fault capabilities and
+ * register/instruction/interrupt/hardware-error/clock/accelerator manifests,
+ * and binds/seals their initial identities, only under its actual entered
+ * stopped class-0 CPU child. Cached rows do not reopen initial construction;
+ * later access requires a separately authenticated borrower. Failed post
+ * preserves internal construction and binding state plus the Source owner.
+ * The bounded native constructor payer is not installed, so selected factories
+ * currently refuse even under that temporal child. */
+
