+PRIMITIVE(q, uint64_t, 8)
diff --git a/tests/unit/crucible-dirty-iterator.rst b/tests/unit/crucible-dirty-iterator.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..66f492de3e0d862a78371465cb89f511061297a3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/unit/crucible-dirty-iterator.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,1888 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+
+Dirty selection and capture lifecycle qualification
+==================================================
+
+Software APIC timer storage component
+-------------------------------------
+
+The software ``apic`` type now contains its actual ``QEMUTimer`` in a private
+``APICState`` extent. ``APICCommonState`` and the KVM, Xen and WHPX type extents
+are unchanged. The existing selected QOM allocation observer is generic: while
+the real boot construction scope is held, it measures each actual TypeImpl
+class/instance allocation, including an APIC born inside that scope. Its
+instance-size observation therefore includes the inline timer before birth.
+No timer capacity scalar or CPU pin supplies a new payer. Ordinary QOM
+allocation remains ordinary allocation outside that scope.
+
+The actual software realize body initializes this storage with
+``timer_init_ns`` using the same virtual clock, scale, callback and opaque as
+the prior ``timer_new_ns``. Unrealize removes active-list membership, deinitializes
+the timer and clears the optional common pointer. Actual instance finalization
+performs the same idempotent cleanup, including failure inside realize before
+qdev would call unrealize. Storage returns with the complete QOM instance;
+there is no separate heap timer allocation or free. Reinitialization after a
+completed unrealize obtains normal fresh timer initialization. VMState fields,
+timer arithmetic, APIC callbacks and accelerator selection are unchanged.
+
+``test-crucible-apic-timer-storage.py --output-dir PATH`` takes the configured
+target/compiler flags in ``CC``/``CFLAGS`` and the real QOM/timer libraries in
+``LDFLAGS``. It extracts the literal private layout, producer, cleanup,
+unrealize, finalizer and TypeInfo. Real initialized QOM objects and real timer
+initialization/list dispatch/delete/deinitialization execute. A diagnostic
+parent class and callback exclude architecture realization, interrupt effects
+and selected admission. Both ordinary and picosecond timer modes dispatch the
+stored diagnostic callback. Pending unrealize, finalization without unrealize,
+uninitialized finalization, idempotence and reuse are checked. Nine independently
+rebuilt omissions must reach their specific assertion detector; compilation
+failure or an arbitrary crash does not count. The complete configured software
+APIC, common APIC, CPU/APIC binding, x86 register, KVM APIC and QOM production
+objects are separately compiled; that does not execute selected construction.
+
+In the configured x86-64 layout, ``APICCommonState`` remains 5984 bytes and
+``QEMUTimer`` is 112 bytes. The software type grows from 5984 to 6096 bytes,
+with alignment 16 unchanged. The actual generic QOM instance geometry grows
+by 112 bytes for that type; Source allocation-header and native-receipt sizes
+are unchanged. This measures real storage only. It does not establish a
+successful Source debit, constructor borrower or callback physical return.
+
+Remaining architecture read-effect joins
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+``x86_cpu_apic_create`` constructs the selected actual class, parents it as
+``lapic`` under the real CPU and sets its reverse CPU pointer before realize.
+The boot observer begins before machine creation and remains through board and
+CLI device creation and initial-CPU completion. A genuine selected APIC birth
+can thus have a retained generic QOM allocation receipt already; the missing
+Source join must bind that exact receipt/generation and actual CPU/APIC child
+relationship to the same construction Original. Matching snapshots, IDs,
+class names or a retained CPU alone cannot replace that join.
+
+The register CR8 read calls the real ``cpu_get_apic_tpr`` dispatch. Software
+APIC calls ``apic_sync_vapic``: a nonzero VAPIC address performs the actual
+physical-memory read and updates ``s->tpr``. That read can traverse the real
+AddressSpace/FlatView, ordinary RAM, IOMMU or MMIO callbacks. RCU/FlatView and
+MemoryRegion/QOM references supply physical retention edges, not Source
+operation authority, RAM payment or transitive device callback custody. The
+existing RAM-only ``apic_fingerprint_tpr`` cannot replace this callback without
+changing legacy effects. KVM returns ``s->tpr >> 4``, Xen returns zero and WHPX
+returns ``s->tpr``; none is replaced with the software behavior.
+
+Likewise ARM manifest membership excludes ``ARM_CP_NO_RAW`` and
+``ARM_CP_NO_GDB`` but does not prove a raw callback effect-free.
+``read_raw_cp_reg`` preserves constant, raw-read callback, read callback and
+direct-field branches. The actual ``cp_regs`` hash table and allocated
+descriptors need their own constructor/allocator/retirement joins, followed by
+the dependencies reached by the real callbacks. The CPU instance pin does not
+pay these allocations or authorize timer/machine effects.
+
+Finally, ``timer_del`` is not an in-flight callback join: the real timer loop
+copies callback/opaque and releases its list lock before invocation. Clock and
+injector registrations may also retain APIC callbacks beyond list membership.
+Their actual admission, callback first/post and physical return, registration
+retirement and dependent-owner release must join before claiming architecture
+read ownership. This component supplies none of those missing interfaces.
+The existing SDK payment refusal, selected unavailability and runtime
+Original/Advance refusal remain unchanged.
+
+``test-crucible-dirty-iterator.py`` has two obligations. Its literal component
+fixture exercises ``capture_next_page_coordinate``,
+``qemu_crucible_ram_next_dirty_range`` and the real bitmap primitives. Its
+mandatory capture lifecycle obligation requires a launched QEMU with genuine
+Source and Root ownership. The driver deliberately fails after producing
+component evidence because that lifecycle integration is not yet available.
+There is no component-only success option or caller-supplied pass receipt.
+
+The selector has no authority or reader callback. The production public wrapper
+retains admission checks, diagnostics, actual operational reads, generation
+revalidation, fingerprint recording and logical progress. Begin and finish keep
+their real Source operation, logical capture and retirement dependencies. The
+component fixture sets inventory/cursor inputs directly; it issues no owner,
+Original, operation, read receipt, dirty ACK or physical-return claim.
+
+The component matrix retains the page-size, alignment, partial-region,
+bitmap-block/word-boundary and ordered-tuple comparisons against the frozen
+page-by-page algorithm. It retains the four primitive/index/address variants,
+RCU/work counters, overflow and invalid-range checks. Mutation controls verify
+that changing bytes without notification does not select a clean page, full
+selection still enumerates it, explicit notification selects it, and a bitmap
+word observation can expose a changed dirty generation without clearing dirt.
+Generation refusal after that change belongs to the public lifecycle wrapper,
+not the coordinate helper. Public cursor advancement also belongs to that
+wrapper: the component does not synthesize a cursor sequence or claim to check
+``*cursor += 1``. Genuine coverage must observe the caller-owned cursor before
+and after each actual public read, including failures and end of iteration. The component performs no ACK or provider I/O.
+
+Matrix completion is independently required: seven target page sizes times
+three alignments times 257 selections, plus the representable block-boundary,
+word-boundary and oversized-page pairs. That is 5427 comparisons for ordinary
+and modeled-index32 variants, and 5415 for modeled RAM-address32 (only one
+block-boundary size is representable). Both the component and driver check
+these fixed dimensions. The later notification control adds exactly one case.
+A causal negative control removes only the matrix call and invokes that
+compiled component directly; it must reach its specific matrix-coverage
+failure. A compiler failure, arbitrary component crash or the driver's final
+mandatory lifecycle failure never counts as that detector firing.
+
+
+Remaining mandatory integration seam
+------------------------------------
+
+The obsolete primitive-only lifecycle C fixture is removed. Its successful
+admission/read/rearm stand-ins could not authenticate today's Source operation,
+logical capture, Root writer or retirement borrower. Its selector matrix,
+invalid-range and overflow checks, RCU/work counters and bitmap/byte-mutation
+controls remain in the literal component. Its lifecycle negative and cleanup
+obligations remain mandatory below. The explicit failing driver is the
+outstanding gate; component success never qualifies those obligations.
+
+The replacement cohort must launch the real emulator and matched module through
+real preexec/Source activation and admission, then enter the actual Source
+operation and Root/writer cut. It must exercise the existing public capture
+entry/read/finish paths and retain independently observed operation, callback,
+post, rearm, logical-ACK and physical-return outcomes. No successful provider
+stub, token, bare begin/finish pair or unsigned test receipt can substitute.
+
+The required scenarios retain these checks:
+
+* Exact ordered coordinates and actual bytes under full and notified capture,
+  including changed bytes without notification and the independent dirty client.
+* Actual public cursor advances exactly once after a successful read and stays
+  unchanged on failure and end of iteration; coordinate counts cannot prove it.
+* Wrong capture generation, foreign diagnostic token, unready root reader,
+  invalid capacity and noncommitting diagnostic capture; refusals leave outputs,
+  cursor and dirty bits as required by the actual public contracts.
+* Read failure and dirty/topology mutation during selection/read, with no ACK,
+  actual owner retention and independent cleanup outcomes.
+* Incomplete traversal refuses commit. Callback or Original-post failure cannot
+  become healthy publication, rearm or dirty ACK.
+* Actual rearm failure retains dirt and sticky first refusal. A bare finish
+  cannot fail and then revive that same identity as healthy. A genuine retained
+  cleanup attempt must not
+  erase failure; any later healthy capture needs its own real fresh admission
+  after physical return. Never revive that failed identity to satisfy a test.
+* Dirty clearing follows successful callback/post and real version checks,
+  touches only the fingerprint client, and retains the required physical
+  return obligations. A later return failure preserves signed failure and
+  required restoration/physical debt rather than accepted ACK. Uncertain
+  cleanup preserves its owner.
+* Abort, stale generation and rejected publication return through genuine
+  Source/Root physical cleanup; destructor/free and a later fresh capture must
+  be corroborated independently of logical acceptance.
+
+No live activation, VM lifecycle, actual concurrent worker or performance
+qualification follows from this source separation. Until the genuine cohort is
+implemented and run, retain the explicit mandatory lifecycle failure.
+
+Nominal publisher subscription and local closure
+-----------------------------------------------
+
+The schema-4 standing declaration binds producer-retention edition 1 to the
+installed standing owner. Before exposing an action that can match a request,
+the producer irrevocably retains every born row, including dirty or unprojected
+rows. A matching published Control request additionally requires its entire
+planned cohort already born, projected and Running. An unsent or partial tail
+cannot supply that completeness argument. Peer death and unknown cleanup never
+certify return. The assigned peer's authenticated local closure is an input to
+the producer's separate retirement operation; it does not retire producer rows.
+
+The actual outside-BQL Ready receive interval captures one prepaid Source
+subscription from the completed reader, canonical module payload, first-bound
+member, assigned mapping and retained standing lender. It retains the exact
+cohort and publication sequence before its independent post. Main may borrow
+that nominal subscription only through its actual canonical handoff and entered
+semantic owner. A sequence-current check is a conservative drift refusal on
+this already retained owner; equal decoded values or sequence numbers cannot
+construct membership. No coherent standing snapshot or renewed clock is taken
+under Main's BQL interval.
+
+The ownership graph keeps the local subscription view separate from its paid
+terminal writer. Actual Main and semantic children close first. The local view
+then closes before Ready's execution dependency and parent handoff return, so
+these lifetimes do not depend cyclically on one another. Actual canonical
+module payload destruction follows. Only after those physical dependencies
+close may the retained assigned writer publish a ``CRUCRET1`` local-return
+record. Its writer keeps delivery, member, mapping and standing lender alive
+through publication uncertainty; delivery identity consumption remains blocked.
+
+The writer observes the Host-owned native-endian hold word at byte 256 and
+requires its exact captured even birth. It never clears that hold. At byte 264,
+it advances the existing big-endian atomic return sequence without resetting or
+wrapping it: even-to-odd CAS, 23 payload-word stores, then odd-to-next-even CAS,
+all sequentially consistent. The 184-byte schema-1 payload retains independent
+first/post failures and the complete born/returned cohort. This cut produces no
+progress witness. Odd, exhausted or interfered publication stays retained and
+uncertain. Successful final CAS is saved before independent post refusal, so a
+negative post cannot resurrect a physically consumed writer. No fallible work
+follows actual delivery identity consumption.
+
+Local closure neither acknowledges the request nor grants publisher credit,
+peer row retirement, operation permission or activation. Park uses its separate
+protected journal and cannot use this Control return codec. The mandatory
+launched Source/Root lifecycle remains required independently.
+
+The subscriber component runs literal Ready/receive/Main/Native return bodies,
+a real C payload journal, QOM references and an actual writable anonymous slot
+mapping. Sealed standing installation, assigned-role installation and semantic
+issuer boundaries are explicit modeled inputs. Its positive and independently
+rebuilt omission controls prove those component cuts only. Genuine semantic
+entry requires the installed complete child's first-bound v5 callback quartet;
+no standalone C journal or decoded action tuple substitutes for that module.
+
+Initial constructor coverage prerequisites
+------------------------------------------
+
+The initial CPU checks in ``crucible-initial-cpu-fixture.inc.h`` are assertions
+for an actual entered callback, not a driver that constructs its authority.
+They have not run in a launched selected-Source lifecycle. The public mandatory
+driver still reports missing integration. It must not be treated as a successful
+installation recipe or a source of activation permission.
+
+A qualifying runner needs the production module and its actual installation
+inputs. The loader must enter that module's real ``qemu_plugin_install`` with
+its retained context and loaded image. The preexec owner must already retain
+the admitted metadata partition, process purpose, exact fixed Native floor and
+live construction Original. That entered construction must issue the actual
+CPU metadata account before CPU allocation, retain the canonical QOM allocation
+receipts and register the module's real callbacks. A synthetic standing file,
