+Caller-owned SHA-256 and system-manifest stream
+----------------------------------------------
+
+``QCryptoSHA256`` contains the chaining state, 64-word message schedule,
+eight-word compression scratch, byte count, one block and active-message flag.
+The in-place API uses no configured crypto backend or dynamic allocation.
+``init`` starts or replaces a message; ``update`` accepts arbitrary chunks,
+including an empty NULL input; ``finalize`` writes exactly 32 bytes and consumes
+the active message. Repeated finalization and updates after finalization refuse
+until another ``init``. Finalization makes no erasure guarantee. The caller
+must exclusively retain actual backing throughout; address, capacity and alias
+checks establish no payer, borrowing authority or guest-operation permission.
+
+Checked state alignment/address overflow, input/output disjointness and the
+SHA-256 limit of ``UINT64_MAX / 8`` message bytes precede mutation. Refusal
+preserves the entire state and output. A caller with invalid readable/writable
+backing or an uninitialized state violates the API preconditions; these checks
+do not authenticate arbitrary pointers. An owner may reuse its storage after
+synchronous physical return, or deliberately reset an active message with
+``init`` when it has exclusive access.
+
+The compression loop is adapted from the already vendored
+``roms/u-boot/lib/libavb/avb_sha256.c``. That copy matches U-Boot commit
+``4d579a4394d665b95c5289b5b7c9ce344e07bf18``, at
+https://github.com/u-boot/u-boot/blob/4d579a4394d665b95c5289b5b7c9ce344e07bf18/lib/libavb/avb_sha256.c.
+The full BSD-3-Clause notice is retained beside the adaptation in
+``crypto/hash.c``; that file retains its existing LGPL-2.1-or-later scope and
+the adapted portion also retains the BSD conditions. No optional dependency
+is added. Existing ``QCryptoHash`` wrappers retain their configured backends.
+
+``qemu_crucible_fault_system_manifest_into_v1`` synchronously consumes the real,
+stable VMState section registry into caller-owned hash/output storage. It
+checks both complete writable extents against each other, the registry
+pointer, array object and pointer rows, every section record and every name
+before resetting the hash. Callers must retain stable registry access under
+the existing QEMU serialization rules. The complete sorted stream is exactly
+each name including NUL followed by its big-endian 32-bit version, without a
+new domain prefix. The registered bounds permit at most twelve sections with
